Refinement status: needs-codex-refinement', 'Signal: source-c4ae562c-e9c1-4f4e-b9e9-dea3e1bcbf40', '2026-05-16-2026-05-15-mcp-server-pitfalls-brief-signal', '2026-05-16-2026-05-15-mcp-server-pitfalls-brief-signal#1');

INSERT INTO chunks (id, document_id, ordinal, heading, text, hash, token_count)
VALUES (
  '2026-05-16-2026-05-15-mcp-server-pitfalls-brief-signal#2', '2026-05-16-2026-05-15-mcp-server-pitfalls-brief-signal', 2, 'Core signal',
  '## Core signal

- MCP tool surface является интерфейсом для недетерминированной модели, поэтому инструменты должны быть сценарными, самодостаточными, семантически ясными, безопасными, тестируемыми через model behavior and bounded by context limits.
- Harness engineering says prompts, skills, tests, lints and review agents are guardrails.
- Unit tests test tool code, not whether the model uses tools correctly; add scenario evals and smoke tests.
- Together they imply: agent tools must be designed, tested and documented as part of the harness, not as incidental API wrappers.
- Prompt injection can enter through user prompts, database/API content and malicious MCP server outputs.
- MCP pitfall analysis says MCP tool schema, descriptions, errors and response shapes are also guardrails.
- 1:1 mapping API endpoints to MCP tools creates tool-selection confusion.
- Error messages should be written as recovery prompts.
- Tool responses must be bounded and paginated to preserve context.
- Add eval fixtures for expected tool choice and parameter shape.', '6e563b0e51a56618726c2728be3e693449cba32cccdbe68824d46892125501b2', 212
);
INSERT INTO chunks_fts (text, heading, document_id, chunk_id)
VALUES ('## Core signal

- MCP tool surface является интерфейсом для недетерминированной модели, поэтому инструменты должны быть сценарными, самодостаточными, семантически ясными, безопасными, тестируемыми через model behavior and bounded by context limits.
- Harness engineering says prompts, skills, tests, lints and review agents are guardrails.
- Unit tests test tool code, not whether the model uses tools correctly; add scenario evals and smoke tests.
- Together they imply: agent tools must be designed, tested and documented as part of the harness, not as incidental API wrappers.
- Prompt injection can enter through user prompts, database/API content and malicious MCP server outputs.
- MCP pitfall analysis says MCP tool schema, descriptions, errors and response shapes are also guardrails.
- 1:1 mapping API endpoints to MCP tools creates tool-selection confusion.
- Error messages should be written as recovery prompts.
- Tool responses must be bounded and paginated to preserve context.
- Add eval fixtures for expected tool choice and parameter shape.', 'Core signal', '2026-05-16-2026-05-15-mcp-server-pitfalls-brief-signal', '2026-05-16-2026-05-15-mcp-server-pitfalls-brief-signal#2');

INSERT INTO chunks (id, document_id, ordinal, heading, text, hash, token_count)
VALUES (
  '2026-05-16-2026-05-15-mcp-server-pitfalls-brief-signal#3', '2026-05-16-2026-05-15-mcp-server-pitfalls-brief-signal', 3, 'Technical details',
  '## Technical details

- Long dependent chains are brittle; prefer high-level tools that hide IDs and sequencing.
- Create `mcp-tool-design` standard before building real MCP servers.
- Главный вывод для Techscope: MCP server нельзя проектировать как обычную API-обертку.
- Авторизация в MCP clients пока неоднородна; remote MCP auth требует client compatibility matrix.', 'cdf7b3771f7e5a38b66c83dc530ac4929f1fba772d847307d6e2f739c0a54c53', 71
);
INSERT INTO chunks_fts (text, heading, document_id, chunk_id)
VALUES ('## Technical details

- Long dependent chains are brittle; prefer high-level tools that hide IDs and sequencing.
- Create `mcp-tool-design` standard before building real MCP servers.
- Главный вывод для Techscope: MCP server нельзя проектировать как обычную API-обертку.
- Авторизация в MCP clients пока неоднородна; remote MCP auth требует client compatibility matrix.', 'Technical details', '2026-05-16-2026-05-15-mcp-server-pitfalls-brief-signal', '2026-05-16-2026-05-15-mcp-server-pitfalls-brief-signal#3');

INSERT INTO chunks (id, document_id, ordinal, heading, text, hash, token_count)
VALUES (
  '2026-05-16-2026-05-15-mcp-server-pitfalls-brief-signal#4', '2026-05-16-2026-05-15-mcp-server-pitfalls-brief-signal', 4, 'Agent design implications',
  '## Agent design implications

- Проверить, можно ли превратить signal в правила для `AGENTS.md`, skills, MCP tools, reviewer agents, evals или workflows.
- Использовать этот signal как сжатый вход для assessment/review, но возвращаться к sources для финальных решений.', '332587e863357025dbfa87a85421c4c5a8ccd2738088112d22110818123417ab', 52
);
INSERT INTO chunks_fts (text, heading, document_id, chunk_id)
VALUES ('## Agent design implications

- Проверить, можно ли превратить signal в правила для `AGENTS.md`, skills, MCP tools, reviewer agents, evals или workflows.
- Использовать этот signal как сжатый вход для assessment/review, но возвращаться к sources для финальных решений.', 'Agent design implications', '2026-05-16-2026-05-15-mcp-server-pitfalls-brief-signal', '2026-05-16-2026-05-15-mcp-server-pitfalls-brief-signal#4');

INSERT INTO chunks (id, document_id, ordinal, heading, text, hash, token_count)
VALUES (
  '2026-05-16-2026-05-15-mcp-server-pitfalls-brief-signal#5', '2026-05-16-2026-05-15-mcp-server-pitfalls-brief-signal', 5, 'Candidate rules',
  '## Candidate rules

- MCP tool surface является интерфейсом для недетерминированной модели, поэтому инструменты должны быть сценарными, самодостаточными, семантически ясными, безопасными, тестируемыми через model behavior and bounded by context limits.
- Together they imply: agent tools must be designed, tested and documented as part of the harness, not as incidental API wrappers.
- Error messages should be written as recovery prompts.
- Tool responses must be bounded and paginated to preserve context.
- Long dependent chains are brittle; prefer high-level tools that hide IDs and sequencing.', '783ce1eab68f01d7ff6de6d269b68206c4e97b55da87b68a6fe7f9dcbd82acd9', 117
);
INSERT INTO chunks_fts (text, heading, document_id, chunk_id)
VALUES ('## Candidate rules

- MCP tool surface является интерфейсом для недетерминированной модели, поэтому инструменты должны быть сценарными, самодостаточными, семантически ясными, безопасными, тестируемыми через model behavior and bounded by context limits.
- Together they imply: agent tools must be designed, tested and documented as part of the harness, not as incidental API wrappers.
- Error messages should be written as recovery prompts.
- Tool responses must be bounded and paginated to preserve context.
- Long dependent chains are brittle; prefer high-level tools that hide IDs and sequencing.', 'Candidate rules', '2026-05-16-2026-05-15-mcp-server-pitfalls-brief-signal', '2026-05-16-2026-05-15-mcp-server-pitfalls-brief-signal#5');

INSERT INTO chunks (id, document_id, ordinal, heading, text, hash, token_count)
VALUES (
  '2026-05-16-2026-05-15-mcp-server-pitfalls-brief-signal#6', '2026-05-16-2026-05-15-mcp-server-pitfalls-brief-signal', 6, 'Noise removed',
  '## Noise removed

- Вступления, повторы, рекламные блоки, stage banter and generic motivation are intentionally excluded.', 'fb61d9ac34cbc6ae02b55fe6ec1d7ec526ea5f09e59052d4a7c01d8b31f26efd', 22
);
INSERT INTO chunks_fts (text, heading, document_id, chunk_id)
VALUES ('## Noise removed

