Refinement status: codex-refined', 'Signal: source-f6f4ae38-ccc1-4c0e-b595-bd2141b23acd', '2026-05-17-2026-05-17-telegram-telegram-user-49-кстати-codex-умеет-сам-делать-скриншоты-приложений-на-те-signal', '2026-05-17-2026-05-17-telegram-telegram-user-49-кстати-codex-умеет-сам-делать-скриншоты-приложений-на-те-signal#1');

INSERT INTO chunks (id, document_id, ordinal, heading, text, hash, token_count)
VALUES (
  '2026-05-17-2026-05-17-telegram-telegram-user-49-кстати-codex-умеет-сам-делать-скриншоты-приложений-на-те-signal#2', '2026-05-17-2026-05-17-telegram-telegram-user-49-кстати-codex-умеет-сам-делать-скриншоты-приложений-на-те-signal', 2, 'Core signal',
  '## Core signal

- Telegram post and screenshot show Codex working on a mobile UI task while an iPhone Simulator is visible and a captured screenshot appears inside the Codex thread.
- The practical signal is not just "screenshots exist"; it is that a coding agent can close the UI-debug feedback loop by inspecting app state, running commands, taking/reading screenshots and continuing the fix without the user manually copying visual evidence.
- This matters for future iOS/mobile agents: visual state should be a normal artifact in the coding loop, alongside terminal output, file diffs and tests.
- The post claims Codex can do this without extra manual setup, likely through local Xcode/iOS Simulator tooling. Treat the exact implementation as local-environment dependent until tested.
- Official OpenAI release notes for 2026-05-14 confirm Codex mobile/remote surfaces include screenshots, terminal output, diffs, test results and approvals as part of live context.', '1cbfb6dfa5466b168014ccc4dca0fd93b800329e69ff17a3182d445e6518bf74', 200
);
INSERT INTO chunks_fts (text, heading, document_id, chunk_id)
VALUES ('## Core signal

- Telegram post and screenshot show Codex working on a mobile UI task while an iPhone Simulator is visible and a captured screenshot appears inside the Codex thread.
- The practical signal is not just "screenshots exist"; it is that a coding agent can close the UI-debug feedback loop by inspecting app state, running commands, taking/reading screenshots and continuing the fix without the user manually copying visual evidence.
- This matters for future iOS/mobile agents: visual state should be a normal artifact in the coding loop, alongside terminal output, file diffs and tests.
- The post claims Codex can do this without extra manual setup, likely through local Xcode/iOS Simulator tooling. Treat the exact implementation as local-environment dependent until tested.
- Official OpenAI release notes for 2026-05-14 confirm Codex mobile/remote surfaces include screenshots, terminal output, diffs, test results and approvals as part of live context.', 'Core signal', '2026-05-17-2026-05-17-telegram-telegram-user-49-кстати-codex-умеет-сам-делать-скриншоты-приложений-на-те-signal', '2026-05-17-2026-05-17-telegram-telegram-user-49-кстати-codex-умеет-сам-делать-скриншоты-приложений-на-те-signal#2');

INSERT INTO chunks (id, document_id, ordinal, heading, text, hash, token_count)
VALUES (
  '2026-05-17-2026-05-17-telegram-telegram-user-49-кстати-codex-умеет-сам-делать-скриншоты-приложений-на-те-signal#3', '2026-05-17-2026-05-17-telegram-telegram-user-49-кстати-codex-умеет-сам-делать-скриншоты-приложений-на-те-signal', 3, 'Technical details',
  '## Technical details

- Visible screenshot context:
  - task title: `Plan UI and onboarding updates`;
  - Codex reports preference state such as `hasSeenOnboarding = true`;
  - Codex ran multiple commands and is inspecting local app state;
  - iPhone 17 Pro simulator is open with a `Library` screen and `Choose a Photo` CTA;
  - Codex displays a screenshot thumbnail in its thread.
- Apple Simulator docs support screenshot/video capture from Simulator; Codex likely uses local tools/automation around this capability rather than a model-only visual trick.', '67c68a307ef4f39b0aeeaf445a1dcde0bc9e7278af865bdbe56285c146c8eeb4', 114
);
INSERT INTO chunks_fts (text, heading, document_id, chunk_id)
VALUES ('## Technical details

- Visible screenshot context:
  - task title: `Plan UI and onboarding updates`;
  - Codex reports preference state such as `hasSeenOnboarding = true`;
  - Codex ran multiple commands and is inspecting local app state;
  - iPhone 17 Pro simulator is open with a `Library` screen and `Choose a Photo` CTA;
  - Codex displays a screenshot thumbnail in its thread.
- Apple Simulator docs support screenshot/video capture from Simulator; Codex likely uses local tools/automation around this capability rather than a model-only visual trick.', 'Technical details', '2026-05-17-2026-05-17-telegram-telegram-user-49-кстати-codex-умеет-сам-делать-скриншоты-приложений-на-те-signal', '2026-05-17-2026-05-17-telegram-telegram-user-49-кстати-codex-умеет-сам-делать-скриншоты-приложений-на-те-signal#3');

INSERT INTO chunks (id, document_id, ordinal, heading, text, hash, token_count)
VALUES (
  '2026-05-17-2026-05-17-telegram-telegram-user-49-кстати-codex-умеет-сам-делать-скриншоты-приложений-на-те-signal#4', '2026-05-17-2026-05-17-telegram-telegram-user-49-кстати-codex-умеет-сам-делать-скриншоты-приложений-на-те-signal', 4, 'Agent design implications',
  '## Agent design implications

- For mobile app development agents, define screenshot artifacts as first-class evidence.
- UI debugging workflow should include:
  - launch app/simulator;
  - drive or inspect state;
  - capture screenshot;
  - reason over screenshot;
  - patch code/state;
  - repeat until screenshot and tests match expected state.
- A future Techscope iOS-agent harness should expose a safe screenshot command and preserve screenshots as raw artifacts, not paste them into long Markdown.
- Compare this against Claude Code and other agents as an agent-shell-evaluation dimension: visual feedback loop support.', 'c46027a6f72f55b04318f4c7bc81ca0925871d46ca86c14d572d83d1bc74a3ae', 122
);
INSERT INTO chunks_fts (text, heading, document_id, chunk_id)
VALUES ('## Agent design implications

- For mobile app development agents, define screenshot artifacts as first-class evidence.
- UI debugging workflow should include:
  - launch app/simulator;
  - drive or inspect state;
  - capture screenshot;
  - reason over screenshot;
  - patch code/state;
  - repeat until screenshot and tests match expected state.
- A future Techscope iOS-agent harness should expose a safe screenshot command and preserve screenshots as raw artifacts, not paste them into long Markdown.
- Compare this against Claude Code and other agents as an agent-shell-evaluation dimension: visual feedback loop support.', 'Agent design implications', '2026-05-17-2026-05-17-telegram-telegram-user-49-кстати-codex-умеет-сам-делать-скриншоты-приложений-на-те-signal', '2026-05-17-2026-05-17-telegram-telegram-user-49-кстати-codex-умеет-сам-делать-скриншоты-приложений-на-те-signal#4');

INSERT INTO chunks (id, document_id, ordinal, heading, text, hash, token_count)
VALUES (
  '2026-05-17-2026-05-17-telegram-telegram-user-49-кстати-codex-умеет-сам-делать-скриншоты-приложений-на-те-signal#5', '2026-05-17-2026-05-17-telegram-telegram-user-49-кстати-codex-умеет-сам-делать-скриншоты-приложений-на-те-signal', 5, 'Candidate rules',
  '## Candidate rules

- If a task touches UI, the agent should capture or request visual evidence before claiming the UI is fixed.
- Screenshot-based claims must be linked to raw image files and, where possible, reproduced with commands or tests.
- For iOS work, prefer scripted simulator screenshots over manual screenshots so the workflow is repeatable.
- Do not store app screenshots containing secrets, private user data or customer data in indexed briefs; store sanitized signal only.', '4b9fe1140f98787fc734a126eecabed6ce4ab744301da20390dc59983f19bf98', 106
);
INSERT INTO chunks_fts (text, heading, document_id, chunk_id)
VALUES ('## Candidate rules

- If a task touches UI, the agent should capture or request visual evidence before claiming the UI is fixed.
