INSERT INTO chunks (id, document_id, ordinal, heading, text, hash, token_count)
VALUES (
  '2026-06-01-agent-connectivity-progressive-discovery-signal#2', '2026-06-01-agent-connectivity-progressive-discovery-signal', 2, 'Core Signal',
  '## Core Signal

The material refines Pritha''s existing tool-boundary doctrine rather than
replacing it. The useful pattern is a layered connectivity stack:

- Skills carry reusable domain/procedural knowledge.
- MCP provides external connectivity, auth, governance, discovery and audit
  boundaries.
- CLI/computer use provides token-efficient local execution when the model
  already understands the tool.

The new emphasis is progressive discovery: do not load every tool schema into
context by default. Give the agent a catalog/search path so it can discover and
load only the tools or skills needed for the current task.', '7177491bc2e579dc46847fdd3a033fc9bef9cf8e72195c160b3a84f3789cb849', 123
);
INSERT INTO chunks_fts (text, heading, document_id, chunk_id)
VALUES ('## Core Signal

The material refines Pritha''s existing tool-boundary doctrine rather than
replacing it. The useful pattern is a layered connectivity stack:

- Skills carry reusable domain/procedural knowledge.
- MCP provides external connectivity, auth, governance, discovery and audit
  boundaries.
- CLI/computer use provides token-efficient local execution when the model
  already understands the tool.

The new emphasis is progressive discovery: do not load every tool schema into
context by default. Give the agent a catalog/search path so it can discover and
load only the tools or skills needed for the current task.', 'Core Signal', '2026-06-01-agent-connectivity-progressive-discovery-signal', '2026-06-01-agent-connectivity-progressive-discovery-signal#2');

INSERT INTO chunks (id, document_id, ordinal, heading, text, hash, token_count)
VALUES (
  '2026-06-01-agent-connectivity-progressive-discovery-signal#3', '2026-06-01-agent-connectivity-progressive-discovery-signal', 3, 'Useful Delta For Pritha',
  '## Useful Delta For Pritha

- Add `tool_search`/catalog-style discovery as an optional harness pattern for
  tool-heavy child agents.
- Treat code-mode orchestration as a separate, sandboxed capability: useful for
  composing multiple MCP/CLI/API calls, but not safe as an unbounded default.
- Update MCP connector review to look for server discovery metadata, dynamic
  tool lists, registry entries and Skills Over MCP direction.
- Keep MCP Apps/UI resources as watch/experiment unless a child agent explicitly
  needs interactive widgets from an MCP server.', 'a05250b6ee14e0fdd52142267659ef56c7436f0fda97c5a6798468d599f7da08', 108
);
INSERT INTO chunks_fts (text, heading, document_id, chunk_id)
VALUES ('## Useful Delta For Pritha

- Add `tool_search`/catalog-style discovery as an optional harness pattern for
  tool-heavy child agents.
- Treat code-mode orchestration as a separate, sandboxed capability: useful for
  composing multiple MCP/CLI/API calls, but not safe as an unbounded default.
- Update MCP connector review to look for server discovery metadata, dynamic
  tool lists, registry entries and Skills Over MCP direction.
- Keep MCP Apps/UI resources as watch/experiment unless a child agent explicitly
  needs interactive widgets from an MCP server.', 'Useful Delta For Pritha', '2026-06-01-agent-connectivity-progressive-discovery-signal', '2026-06-01-agent-connectivity-progressive-discovery-signal#3');

INSERT INTO chunks (id, document_id, ordinal, heading, text, hash, token_count)
VALUES (
  '2026-06-01-agent-connectivity-progressive-discovery-signal#4', '2026-06-01-agent-connectivity-progressive-discovery-signal', 4, 'Relationship To Existing Memory',
  '## Relationship To Existing Memory

This confirms:

- `agent-tool-integration-selection`: choose CLI, skill, MCP, browser or manual
  by task boundary.
- `agent-mcp-connector-lifecycle`: MCP is optional, reviewed and scoped.
- `agent-skill-pack-lifecycle`: skills are procedural memory and should remain
  progressive-disclosure artifacts.

This refines:

- broad tool schemas are not only a cost problem; they should trigger a
  discovery/catalog design;
- MCP server discovery and Skills Over MCP should be watched as emerging
  interoperability patterns.', '20a935ec092a1c6b33d1e390febfc0a0bd6cc5066ccc141b470f1a54cebea5fd', 96
);
INSERT INTO chunks_fts (text, heading, document_id, chunk_id)
VALUES ('## Relationship To Existing Memory

This confirms:

- `agent-tool-integration-selection`: choose CLI, skill, MCP, browser or manual
  by task boundary.
- `agent-mcp-connector-lifecycle`: MCP is optional, reviewed and scoped.
- `agent-skill-pack-lifecycle`: skills are procedural memory and should remain
  progressive-disclosure artifacts.

This refines:

- broad tool schemas are not only a cost problem; they should trigger a
  discovery/catalog design;
- MCP server discovery and Skills Over MCP should be watched as emerging
  interoperability patterns.', 'Relationship To Existing Memory', '2026-06-01-agent-connectivity-progressive-discovery-signal', '2026-06-01-agent-connectivity-progressive-discovery-signal#4');

INSERT INTO chunks (id, document_id, ordinal, heading, text, hash, token_count)
VALUES (
  '2026-06-01-agent-connectivity-progressive-discovery-signal#5', '2026-06-01-agent-connectivity-progressive-discovery-signal', 5, 'Candidate Rules',
  '## Candidate Rules

- Tool-heavy agents should prefer progressive discovery over eager loading of
  every tool schema.
- If a child agent needs many external tools, add a catalog/search layer before
  adding broad MCP toolsets.
- Code-mode orchestration requires sandboxing, timeout, filesystem/network
  policy and approval gates.
- MCP roadmap claims should be verified against official MCP Roadmap, SEPs or
  WG charters before becoming standards.', '25d45cc7a058eb136de376cc5b50718675eb039a3718e156d6d3d7afe9beea2d', 87
);
INSERT INTO chunks_fts (text, heading, document_id, chunk_id)
VALUES ('## Candidate Rules

- Tool-heavy agents should prefer progressive discovery over eager loading of
  every tool schema.
- If a child agent needs many external tools, add a catalog/search layer before
  adding broad MCP toolsets.
- Code-mode orchestration requires sandboxing, timeout, filesystem/network
  policy and approval gates.
- MCP roadmap claims should be verified against official MCP Roadmap, SEPs or
  WG charters before becoming standards.', 'Candidate Rules', '2026-06-01-agent-connectivity-progressive-discovery-signal', '2026-06-01-agent-connectivity-progressive-discovery-signal#5');

INSERT INTO chunks (id, document_id, ordinal, heading, text, hash, token_count)
VALUES (
  '2026-06-01-agent-connectivity-progressive-discovery-signal#6', '2026-06-01-agent-connectivity-progressive-discovery-signal', 6, 'Verification Notes',
  '## Verification Notes

- Official MCP Roadmap confirms transport/scalability, server cards, enterprise
  readiness and extension ecosystem as active priorities.
- Skills Over MCP is an active working group; current direction is an extension
  using existing Resources primitives.
- Stateless MCP and Server Cards have SEP-level artifacts, but client/server
  support should be rechecked before scaffold decisions.', '4e44c6ef55eb478d0a108e6b384801c32d3ea0fc0d1943fe5faace207a4a66f0', 75
);
