INSERT INTO chunks (id, document_id, ordinal, heading, text, hash, token_count)
VALUES (
  '2026-06-01-media-transcript-auzan-ai-education-human-potential-signal#2', '2026-06-01-media-transcript-auzan-ai-education-human-potential-signal', 2, 'Core signal',
  '## Core signal

- The video is not primarily about programming or agent infrastructure. Its useful Techscope signal is about learning-agent design: if AI can perform the old educational tasks, education and evaluation should move toward human capacities that are harder to outsource.
- Auzan''s proposed direction is to develop "another natural intelligence" for the AI era: intuition under uncertainty, empathy, imagination, memory/system thinking and critical thinking toward AI.
- The strongest practical point for agents is assessment design. If tasks can be solved by a hidden AI assistant, the learning system should evaluate process, reasoning, project work, live interaction, critique and transfer, not only final answers.
- For Techscope/Agents Mother this is a `watch`, not `adopt`: useful for future learning agents and user-training workflows, but too non-technical and evidence-light to change standards now.', 'a9d651b252de6f9b4d00847c0609617f652818c1f7e334f6547a24301d305b2c', 181
);
INSERT INTO chunks_fts (text, heading, document_id, chunk_id)
VALUES ('## Core signal

- The video is not primarily about programming or agent infrastructure. Its useful Techscope signal is about learning-agent design: if AI can perform the old educational tasks, education and evaluation should move toward human capacities that are harder to outsource.
- Auzan''s proposed direction is to develop "another natural intelligence" for the AI era: intuition under uncertainty, empathy, imagination, memory/system thinking and critical thinking toward AI.
- The strongest practical point for agents is assessment design. If tasks can be solved by a hidden AI assistant, the learning system should evaluate process, reasoning, project work, live interaction, critique and transfer, not only final answers.
- For Techscope/Agents Mother this is a `watch`, not `adopt`: useful for future learning agents and user-training workflows, but too non-technical and evidence-light to change standards now.', 'Core signal', '2026-06-01-media-transcript-auzan-ai-education-human-potential-signal', '2026-06-01-media-transcript-auzan-ai-education-human-potential-signal#2');

INSERT INTO chunks (id, document_id, ordinal, heading, text, hash, token_count)
VALUES (
  '2026-06-01-media-transcript-auzan-ai-education-human-potential-signal#3', '2026-06-01-media-transcript-auzan-ai-education-human-potential-signal', 3, 'Technical details',
  '## Technical details

- It frames the future split as AI either replacing human capability or extending it; the design lever is how humans are trained to work with AI.
- The five human capacities mentioned as candidates for development are:
  - intuition: decisions under incomplete information and stress;
  - empathy: social understanding that AI can imitate but not truly possess;
  - imagination: ability to generate mental models and future possibilities;
  - memory/system thinking: resistance to fragmented "clip" memory;
  - critical thinking toward AI: ability to question AI output rather than treating it as authority.
- The transcript quality is usable but noisy: ASR produced several name/word errors, so claims should be checked before citation.', '158ee1149b7aa8ebfd26a91b2f8690cc661d381a95aac512465398d0f2901cb5', 156
);
INSERT INTO chunks_fts (text, heading, document_id, chunk_id)
VALUES ('## Technical details

- It frames the future split as AI either replacing human capability or extending it; the design lever is how humans are trained to work with AI.
- The five human capacities mentioned as candidates for development are:
  - intuition: decisions under incomplete information and stress;
  - empathy: social understanding that AI can imitate but not truly possess;
  - imagination: ability to generate mental models and future possibilities;
  - memory/system thinking: resistance to fragmented "clip" memory;
  - critical thinking toward AI: ability to question AI output rather than treating it as authority.
- The transcript quality is usable but noisy: ASR produced several name/word errors, so claims should be checked before citation.', 'Technical details', '2026-06-01-media-transcript-auzan-ai-education-human-potential-signal', '2026-06-01-media-transcript-auzan-ai-education-human-potential-signal#3');

INSERT INTO chunks (id, document_id, ordinal, heading, text, hash, token_count)
VALUES (
  '2026-06-01-media-transcript-auzan-ai-education-human-potential-signal#4', '2026-06-01-media-transcript-auzan-ai-education-human-potential-signal', 4, 'Agent design implications',
  '## Agent design implications

- Learning agents should avoid becoming answer vending machines. They should ask users to predict, explain, critique, compare, reconstruct and transfer knowledge.
- Future tutoring/scaffold agents should include AI-output critique drills: ask the learner to find errors, missing assumptions, overconfidence and unsupported claims in model answers.
- Training workflows for users of Pritha descendants should include explicit "when not to trust the agent" material, not just command instructions.
- Evaluation tasks for educational agents should include process evidence: intermediate reasoning, oral/live checks, project artifacts, reflection and human review gates.', '9987b380abe06efa098c2c16425d3f6196126321d9ef96de59861eb55a984608', 126
);
INSERT INTO chunks_fts (text, heading, document_id, chunk_id)
VALUES ('## Agent design implications

- Learning agents should avoid becoming answer vending machines. They should ask users to predict, explain, critique, compare, reconstruct and transfer knowledge.
- Future tutoring/scaffold agents should include AI-output critique drills: ask the learner to find errors, missing assumptions, overconfidence and unsupported claims in model answers.
- Training workflows for users of Pritha descendants should include explicit "when not to trust the agent" material, not just command instructions.
- Evaluation tasks for educational agents should include process evidence: intermediate reasoning, oral/live checks, project artifacts, reflection and human review gates.', 'Agent design implications', '2026-06-01-media-transcript-auzan-ai-education-human-potential-signal', '2026-06-01-media-transcript-auzan-ai-education-human-potential-signal#4');

INSERT INTO chunks (id, document_id, ordinal, heading, text, hash, token_count)
VALUES (
  '2026-06-01-media-transcript-auzan-ai-education-human-potential-signal#5', '2026-06-01-media-transcript-auzan-ai-education-human-potential-signal', 5, 'Candidate rules',
  '## Candidate rules

- Do not measure learning-agent success only by whether the user reaches a correct final answer.
- In learning workflows, preserve friction that develops judgment: prediction before answer, critique before acceptance, and reflection after tool use.
- Add AI-critical-thinking exercises when an agent teaches or trains a user to rely on AI tools.
- Treat education/future-of-work videos as supporting context unless they provide concrete methods, evals or primary evidence.', '582b84018c697f52548df7d53b4e8d380181442c5ab1ea8e6ac3f25b9d272c7d', 98
);
INSERT INTO chunks_fts (text, heading, document_id, chunk_id)
VALUES ('## Candidate rules

- Do not measure learning-agent success only by whether the user reaches a correct final answer.
