INSERT INTO chunks_fts (text, heading, document_id, chunk_id)
VALUES ('# Signal: JS/TS Agent UI Framework Source Batch

Date: 2026-06-02
Status: refined
Source class: mixed
Retention: source-purged', 'Signal: JS/TS Agent UI Framework Source Batch', '2026-06-02-js-ts-agent-ui-framework-source-batch-signal', '2026-06-02-js-ts-agent-ui-framework-source-batch-signal#1');

INSERT INTO chunks (id, document_id, ordinal, heading, text, hash, token_count)
VALUES (
  '2026-06-02-js-ts-agent-ui-framework-source-batch-signal#2', '2026-06-02-js-ts-agent-ui-framework-source-batch-signal', 2, 'Core Signal',
  '## Core Signal

Most JavaScript/TypeScript "agent framework" materials are about backend
orchestration, not UI. For Pritha''s interface layer, the useful adoption signal
is narrower: when a child agent needs a web/chat/workflow UI in the
JavaScript/TypeScript ecosystem, choose a frontend framework and AI UI layer
based on streaming state, typed tool parts, user controls, approvals,
cancellation, persistence and the existing app stack.', 'eff3a28400c17d9ecfd132fa3b6f9358e1419f3d94ef161da1eb0937923b768c', 83
);
INSERT INTO chunks_fts (text, heading, document_id, chunk_id)
VALUES ('## Core Signal

Most JavaScript/TypeScript "agent framework" materials are about backend
orchestration, not UI. For Pritha''s interface layer, the useful adoption signal
is narrower: when a child agent needs a web/chat/workflow UI in the
JavaScript/TypeScript ecosystem, choose a frontend framework and AI UI layer
based on streaming state, typed tool parts, user controls, approvals,
cancellation, persistence and the existing app stack.', 'Core Signal', '2026-06-02-js-ts-agent-ui-framework-source-batch-signal', '2026-06-02-js-ts-agent-ui-framework-source-batch-signal#2');

INSERT INTO chunks (id, document_id, ordinal, heading, text, hash, token_count)
VALUES (
  '2026-06-02-js-ts-agent-ui-framework-source-batch-signal#3', '2026-06-02-js-ts-agent-ui-framework-source-batch-signal', 3, 'Useful Delta For Pritha',
  '## Useful Delta For Pritha

- Existing frontend framework wins. Do not switch a child project to a new UI
  framework only because an agent backend framework is popular.
- Vercel AI SDK UI is relevant to the UI layer because it provides frontend
  hooks and framework support for streaming chat, completion, structured data,
  status/error state and tool/generative UI rendering.
- AI SDK 6 adds a useful TypeScript pattern: one typed tool/agent definition can
  feed API routes and UI tool components, reducing mismatch between agent logic
  and rendered UI state.
- UI framework selection should not be confused with choosing LangChain.js,
  Google ADK TS, OpenAI Agents SDK TS or Mastra. Those are harness/runtime
  choices unless the contract specifically asks for their frontend integration.
- UI requirements should be expressed in user-facing terms: status states,
  stop/regenerate, approval prompts, typed tool cards, attachments, error
  handling, stream resumption and mobile/accessibility behavior.', '657a9cb02a8d015ca4b7c22be40f3341e1915cd0b6342328681aa8f8563198ef', 200
);
INSERT INTO chunks_fts (text, heading, document_id, chunk_id)
VALUES ('## Useful Delta For Pritha

- Existing frontend framework wins. Do not switch a child project to a new UI
  framework only because an agent backend framework is popular.
- Vercel AI SDK UI is relevant to the UI layer because it provides frontend
  hooks and framework support for streaming chat, completion, structured data,
  status/error state and tool/generative UI rendering.
- AI SDK 6 adds a useful TypeScript pattern: one typed tool/agent definition can
  feed API routes and UI tool components, reducing mismatch between agent logic
  and rendered UI state.
- UI framework selection should not be confused with choosing LangChain.js,
  Google ADK TS, OpenAI Agents SDK TS or Mastra. Those are harness/runtime
  choices unless the contract specifically asks for their frontend integration.
- UI requirements should be expressed in user-facing terms: status states,
  stop/regenerate, approval prompts, typed tool cards, attachments, error
  handling, stream resumption and mobile/accessibility behavior.', 'Useful Delta For Pritha', '2026-06-02-js-ts-agent-ui-framework-source-batch-signal', '2026-06-02-js-ts-agent-ui-framework-source-batch-signal#3');

INSERT INTO chunks (id, document_id, ordinal, heading, text, hash, token_count)
VALUES (
  '2026-06-02-js-ts-agent-ui-framework-source-batch-signal#4', '2026-06-02-js-ts-agent-ui-framework-source-batch-signal', 4, 'Pritha Rule Candidate',
  '## Pritha Rule Candidate

When a child agent selects web/workflow UI, Pritha should ask:

- Is there an existing frontend framework?
- Is the UI chat-like, workflow-like, dashboard-like or embedded?
- Does it need streaming messages or streaming structured data?
- Does it render tool calls as components?
- Does it need approval controls before tool execution?
- Does it need stop/regenerate/resume/persist behavior?
- Which UI kit/framework owns design, accessibility and mobile behavior?', 'cd04b1a755aead15fa7f62d8dacbcd5330c8ff378d6f669a3808df19f17c8f12', 99
);
INSERT INTO chunks_fts (text, heading, document_id, chunk_id)
VALUES ('## Pritha Rule Candidate

When a child agent selects web/workflow UI, Pritha should ask:

- Is there an existing frontend framework?
- Is the UI chat-like, workflow-like, dashboard-like or embedded?
- Does it need streaming messages or streaming structured data?
- Does it render tool calls as components?
- Does it need approval controls before tool execution?
- Does it need stop/regenerate/resume/persist behavior?
- Which UI kit/framework owns design, accessibility and mobile behavior?', 'Pritha Rule Candidate', '2026-06-02-js-ts-agent-ui-framework-source-batch-signal', '2026-06-02-js-ts-agent-ui-framework-source-batch-signal#4');

INSERT INTO chunks (id, document_id, ordinal, heading, text, hash, token_count)
VALUES (
  '2026-06-02-js-ts-agent-ui-framework-source-batch-signal#5', '2026-06-02-js-ts-agent-ui-framework-source-batch-signal', 5, 'Noise Removed',
  '## Noise Removed

- Backend agent framework comparisons are not promoted as UI framework rules.
- Node.js/TypeScript popularity is not treated as a UI decision.
- Persistent memory examples are not promoted into UI guidance unless they
  create explicit user-facing memory controls.', '927283b4699b58b0eea1b93bb27341186b7155efda01302cbfed3b8ad41bae35', 57
);
INSERT INTO chunks_fts (text, heading, document_id, chunk_id)
VALUES ('## Noise Removed

- Backend agent framework comparisons are not promoted as UI framework rules.
- Node.js/TypeScript popularity is not treated as a UI decision.
