INSERT INTO chunks (id, document_id, ordinal, heading, text, hash, token_count)
VALUES (
  '2026-05-17-openclaw-hermes-codex-cli-advanced-user-brief#2', '2026-05-17-openclaw-hermes-codex-cli-advanced-user-brief', 2, 'Summary',
  '## Summary

Видео полезно как UX-свидетельство продвинутого пользователя, который не является профессиональным разработчиком, но активно использует агентские системы. Его главный практический вывод: выбор агентской среды для реальной работы определяется не "самым умным" ответом, а стабильностью контура, управлением памятью, стоимостью контекста, прозрачностью tools/skills and recovery after restart.', 'e2b469e8bc3a1ea42ed1bff2a22c8f14f36ac14faaf3265e9c5486e80a5bba32', 63
);
INSERT INTO chunks_fts (text, heading, document_id, chunk_id)
VALUES ('## Summary

Видео полезно как UX-свидетельство продвинутого пользователя, который не является профессиональным разработчиком, но активно использует агентские системы. Его главный практический вывод: выбор агентской среды для реальной работы определяется не "самым умным" ответом, а стабильностью контура, управлением памятью, стоимостью контекста, прозрачностью tools/skills and recovery after restart.', 'Summary', '2026-05-17-openclaw-hermes-codex-cli-advanced-user-brief', '2026-05-17-openclaw-hermes-codex-cli-advanced-user-brief#2');

INSERT INTO chunks (id, document_id, ordinal, heading, text, hash, token_count)
VALUES (
  '2026-05-17-openclaw-hermes-codex-cli-advanced-user-brief#3', '2026-05-17-openclaw-hermes-codex-cli-advanced-user-brief', 3, 'Key claims',
  '## Key claims

- Agent shells differ mainly by harness thickness: how much context, tools, persona and memory they inject before the model answers.
- Rich/personal shells can be pleasant for individual use, but may accumulate context and become costly or unstable under heavy customization.
- Hermes-like self-improving skill workflows are attractive for business/autonomous tasks, but the claim must be verified against official Hermes docs and observed behavior.
- For non-coders, a useful agent must accept ordinary requests through Telegram or another familiar UI and hide command-line repair work.', '05f471eb6fae73bca6a9588523b63e79ce434778a389fb20cf1179bac073aac3', 121
);
INSERT INTO chunks_fts (text, heading, document_id, chunk_id)
VALUES ('## Key claims

- Agent shells differ mainly by harness thickness: how much context, tools, persona and memory they inject before the model answers.
- Rich/personal shells can be pleasant for individual use, but may accumulate context and become costly or unstable under heavy customization.
- Hermes-like self-improving skill workflows are attractive for business/autonomous tasks, but the claim must be verified against official Hermes docs and observed behavior.
- For non-coders, a useful agent must accept ordinary requests through Telegram or another familiar UI and hide command-line repair work.', 'Key claims', '2026-05-17-openclaw-hermes-codex-cli-advanced-user-brief', '2026-05-17-openclaw-hermes-codex-cli-advanced-user-brief#3');

INSERT INTO chunks (id, document_id, ordinal, heading, text, hash, token_count)
VALUES (
  '2026-05-17-openclaw-hermes-codex-cli-advanced-user-brief#4', '2026-05-17-openclaw-hermes-codex-cli-advanced-user-brief', 4, 'Evidence',
  '## Evidence

- Karpathy LLM Wiki gist, 2026-04-04, describes raw sources, generated wiki and schema as separate layers, with index/log operations.
- NousResearch `hermes-agent` repo describes skill learning, multi-provider support, gateways, memory/search and subagent delegation.
- Hermes Codex runtime docs say Codex app-server integration is opt-in and that some Hermes loop tools such as delegate_task/memory/session_search/todo are not available in stateless Codex runtime mode.
- OpenAI Codex repo/docs position Codex CLI as a local coding agent; OpenAI Codex app article frames app/CLI/IDE/cloud as related but distinct surfaces.
- arXiv memory survey frames agent memory as a write-manage-read loop and highlights privacy governance, contradiction handling and latency budgets.
- Community reports found during web check broadly match the "thin wrapper vs heavy shell" tension: some users prefer Codex as the core agent with a small messaging wrapper, while some Hermes/OpenClaw switchers report mixed results around setup, bloat and token usage.', 'c6eb7b85a9942a11325bc54f654f432e8845deb8d70dbb27ad22e72d949f4c05', 200
);
INSERT INTO chunks_fts (text, heading, document_id, chunk_id)
VALUES ('## Evidence

- Karpathy LLM Wiki gist, 2026-04-04, describes raw sources, generated wiki and schema as separate layers, with index/log operations.
- NousResearch `hermes-agent` repo describes skill learning, multi-provider support, gateways, memory/search and subagent delegation.
- Hermes Codex runtime docs say Codex app-server integration is opt-in and that some Hermes loop tools such as delegate_task/memory/session_search/todo are not available in stateless Codex runtime mode.
- OpenAI Codex repo/docs position Codex CLI as a local coding agent; OpenAI Codex app article frames app/CLI/IDE/cloud as related but distinct surfaces.
- arXiv memory survey frames agent memory as a write-manage-read loop and highlights privacy governance, contradiction handling and latency budgets.
- Community reports found during web check broadly match the "thin wrapper vs heavy shell" tension: some users prefer Codex as the core agent with a small messaging wrapper, while some Hermes/OpenClaw switchers report mixed results around setup, bloat and token usage.', 'Evidence', '2026-05-17-openclaw-hermes-codex-cli-advanced-user-brief', '2026-05-17-openclaw-hermes-codex-cli-advanced-user-brief#4');

INSERT INTO chunks (id, document_id, ordinal, heading, text, hash, token_count)
VALUES (
  '2026-05-17-openclaw-hermes-codex-cli-advanced-user-brief#5', '2026-05-17-openclaw-hermes-codex-cli-advanced-user-brief', 5, 'Risks and caveats',
  '## Risks and caveats

- Exact "OpenClaw/OpenClow/Crab" identity is unclear and must be pinned before project-specific conclusions.
- Some web sources around OpenClaw/Hermes look promotional or inconsistent; prefer official repo/docs and dated community reports.
- Self-improving skills and auto-written wiki memory increase stale-memory, prompt-injection and accidental-permission risks.
- Business/CRM agent recommendations need separate privacy/security review before implementation.', '89635a3b21722170026a4b237000406ff2047aa32e8d8b421bc478f9604bb892', 77
);
INSERT INTO chunks_fts (text, heading, document_id, chunk_id)
VALUES ('## Risks and caveats

- Exact "OpenClaw/OpenClow/Crab" identity is unclear and must be pinned before project-specific conclusions.
- Some web sources around OpenClaw/Hermes look promotional or inconsistent; prefer official repo/docs and dated community reports.
- Self-improving skills and auto-written wiki memory increase stale-memory, prompt-injection and accidental-permission risks.
- Business/CRM agent recommendations need separate privacy/security review before implementation.', 'Risks and caveats', '2026-05-17-openclaw-hermes-codex-cli-advanced-user-brief', '2026-05-17-openclaw-hermes-codex-cli-advanced-user-brief#5');

INSERT INTO chunks (id, document_id, ordinal, heading, text, hash, token_count)
VALUES (
  '2026-05-17-openclaw-hermes-codex-cli-advanced-user-brief#6', '2026-05-17-openclaw-hermes-codex-cli-advanced-user-brief', 6, 'Recommendation',
  '## Recommendation

Accept as a significant UX/adoption signal. Do not convert directly into a standard.

Add a reusable comparison rubric for future agent architecture materials:

- operator type: coder, semi-technical, non-technical;
- runtime/shell: Codex CLI, Codex app, Hermes, OpenClaw, Claude Code, Gemini CLI, etc.;
- cold-start context and context growth;
- memory model and write policy;
- tool/skill transparency;
- long-task reliability;
- recovery path after bad state;
- cost predictability;
- security boundary and approval model;', '88ffd707542f178172d4dd7b621db9a227859207613cb4ab55a64b5e1f7c0ba0', 104
);
INSERT INTO chunks_fts (text, heading, document_id, chunk_id)
VALUES ('## Recommendation

Accept as a significant UX/adoption signal. Do not convert directly into a standard.

Add a reusable comparison rubric for future agent architecture materials:

- operator type: coder, semi-technical, non-technical;
- runtime/shell: Codex CLI, Codex app, Hermes, OpenClaw, Claude Code, Gemini CLI, etc.;
- cold-start context and context growth;
- memory model and write policy;
- tool/skill transparency;
- long-task reliability;
- recovery path after bad state;
- cost predictability;
- security boundary and approval model;', 'Recommendation', '2026-05-17-openclaw-hermes-codex-cli-advanced-user-brief', '2026-05-17-openclaw-hermes-codex-cli-advanced-user-brief#6');

