- named trusted-operator security model.

Do not turn this into a Techscope standard yet. The next useful step is a review comparing OpenClaw with other popular autonomous agent systems and extracting reusable design rules.', 'Recommendation', '2026-05-17-openclaw-personal-agent-architecture-brief', '2026-05-17-openclaw-personal-agent-architecture-brief#14');

INSERT INTO chunks (id, document_id, ordinal, heading, text, hash, token_count)
VALUES (
  '2026-05-17-openclaw-personal-agent-architecture-brief#15', '2026-05-17-openclaw-personal-agent-architecture-brief', 15, 'Next step',
  '## Next step

- Study 2-3 other autonomous agent architectures.
- Compare against OpenClaw along the axes: ingress, runtime, memory, tools, permissions, sandboxing, multi-agent routing, deployment, evals and recovery.
- If the same patterns recur, promote them into a draft standard for "local-first autonomous agent architecture".', 'c9242cb25c8ad26daa544f022cf689e7fd399e23995dc2be3898ba01bf4cbebf', 63
);
