INSERT INTO chunks_fts (text, heading, document_id, chunk_id)
VALUES ('# Brief: NVIDIA NemoClaw sandboxed agent runtime

Date: 2026-05-27
Source: https://github.com/NVIDIA/NemoClaw
Status: draft', 'Brief: NVIDIA NemoClaw sandboxed agent runtime', 'brief-nvidia-nemoclaw-sandboxed-agent-runtime-2026-05-27', 'brief-nvidia-nemoclaw-sandboxed-agent-runtime-2026-05-27#1');

INSERT INTO chunks (id, document_id, ordinal, heading, text, hash, token_count)
VALUES (
  'brief-nvidia-nemoclaw-sandboxed-agent-runtime-2026-05-27#2', 'brief-nvidia-nemoclaw-sandboxed-agent-runtime-2026-05-27', 2, 'Summary',
  '## Summary

NemoClaw is useful to Techscope primarily as a reference architecture for sandboxing always-on agents, not as a default stack to install. The new reusable idea is a strict runtime boundary: host-side operator/control plane, sandboxed agent process, gateway-held credentials, deny-by-default egress, declarative policy presets, lifecycle logs/status and routed inference.', 'a090b913a190b32139bda93fbfc3699f14347fb5061d58f40bf2481622de4bf0', 68
);
INSERT INTO chunks_fts (text, heading, document_id, chunk_id)
VALUES ('## Summary

NemoClaw is useful to Techscope primarily as a reference architecture for sandboxing always-on agents, not as a default stack to install. The new reusable idea is a strict runtime boundary: host-side operator/control plane, sandboxed agent process, gateway-held credentials, deny-by-default egress, declarative policy presets, lifecycle logs/status and routed inference.', 'Summary', 'brief-nvidia-nemoclaw-sandboxed-agent-runtime-2026-05-27', 'brief-nvidia-nemoclaw-sandboxed-agent-runtime-2026-05-27#2');

INSERT INTO chunks (id, document_id, ordinal, heading, text, hash, token_count)
VALUES (
  'brief-nvidia-nemoclaw-sandboxed-agent-runtime-2026-05-27#3', 'brief-nvidia-nemoclaw-sandboxed-agent-runtime-2026-05-27', 3, 'Key claims',
  '## Key claims

- Always-on agents need a runtime boundary because they can access network, tools, files, credentials and messaging channels for long periods.
- The agent should not hold raw provider keys. A gateway or host-side control plane should inject credentials only at the network boundary.
- External network access should start deny-by-default, then be explicitly allowed by host, method/path, binary and task need.
- Messaging channels such as Telegram/Discord/Slack should be explicit interface adapters with their own policy presets, not implicit global network access.
- Model routing can live outside the agent process: the agent calls a local inference route, while the host chooses provider/model.
- Blueprint/versioned runtime setup is safer than ad hoc manual setup for repeatable agents.', '923a61202f348c7cafbcab68140dcd71972339433280c72a919ab3f08d428231', 164
);
INSERT INTO chunks_fts (text, heading, document_id, chunk_id)
VALUES ('## Key claims

- Always-on agents need a runtime boundary because they can access network, tools, files, credentials and messaging channels for long periods.
- The agent should not hold raw provider keys. A gateway or host-side control plane should inject credentials only at the network boundary.
- External network access should start deny-by-default, then be explicitly allowed by host, method/path, binary and task need.
- Messaging channels such as Telegram/Discord/Slack should be explicit interface adapters with their own policy presets, not implicit global network access.
- Model routing can live outside the agent process: the agent calls a local inference route, while the host chooses provider/model.
- Blueprint/versioned runtime setup is safer than ad hoc manual setup for repeatable agents.', 'Key claims', 'brief-nvidia-nemoclaw-sandboxed-agent-runtime-2026-05-27', 'brief-nvidia-nemoclaw-sandboxed-agent-runtime-2026-05-27#3');

INSERT INTO chunks (id, document_id, ordinal, heading, text, hash, token_count)
VALUES (
  'brief-nvidia-nemoclaw-sandboxed-agent-runtime-2026-05-27#4', 'brief-nvidia-nemoclaw-sandboxed-agent-runtime-2026-05-27', 4, 'Agent environment profile',
  '## Agent environment profile

- Agent platforms: OpenClaw/OpenShell directly; Codex indirectly by architecture pattern.
- Model context: hosted and local inference behind a gateway; optional routed inference.
- Runtime environment: host process + Docker/OpenShell sandbox + gateway.
- Config surfaces: YAML blueprints, network policy, model router config, CLI lifecycle commands.
- Portability: adapter-needed. Concepts port cleanly; NemoClaw implementation is OpenClaw/OpenShell-specific.', '5512c50f87426a332f10cb03166e29004f53ba4676f3e3ca464fdf94ad910c1e', 81
);
INSERT INTO chunks_fts (text, heading, document_id, chunk_id)
VALUES ('## Agent environment profile

- Agent platforms: OpenClaw/OpenShell directly; Codex indirectly by architecture pattern.
- Model context: hosted and local inference behind a gateway; optional routed inference.
- Runtime environment: host process + Docker/OpenShell sandbox + gateway.
- Config surfaces: YAML blueprints, network policy, model router config, CLI lifecycle commands.
- Portability: adapter-needed. Concepts port cleanly; NemoClaw implementation is OpenClaw/OpenShell-specific.', 'Agent environment profile', 'brief-nvidia-nemoclaw-sandboxed-agent-runtime-2026-05-27', 'brief-nvidia-nemoclaw-sandboxed-agent-runtime-2026-05-27#4');

INSERT INTO chunks (id, document_id, ordinal, heading, text, hash, token_count)
VALUES (
  'brief-nvidia-nemoclaw-sandboxed-agent-runtime-2026-05-27#5', 'brief-nvidia-nemoclaw-sandboxed-agent-runtime-2026-05-27', 5, 'Evidence',
  '## Evidence

Official repository and NVIDIA docs confirm:

- alpha status and OpenClaw/OpenShell scope;
- sandbox runtime with Landlock/seccomp/netns and Docker/OpenShell topology;
- gateway-held provider credentials and inference routing via `inference.local`;
- deny-by-default network policy and operator approval flow;
- policy presets for integrations and messaging channels.', '95bca938093cfc3ad484357ad431e0c65ac0c46850c9b2e8d50f67dcb5a244d8', 64
);
INSERT INTO chunks_fts (text, heading, document_id, chunk_id)
VALUES ('## Evidence

Official repository and NVIDIA docs confirm:

- alpha status and OpenClaw/OpenShell scope;
- sandbox runtime with Landlock/seccomp/netns and Docker/OpenShell topology;
- gateway-held provider credentials and inference routing via `inference.local`;
- deny-by-default network policy and operator approval flow;
- policy presets for integrations and messaging channels.', 'Evidence', 'brief-nvidia-nemoclaw-sandboxed-agent-runtime-2026-05-27', 'brief-nvidia-nemoclaw-sandboxed-agent-runtime-2026-05-27#5');

