INSERT INTO chunks (id, document_id, ordinal, heading, text, hash, token_count)
VALUES (
  '2026-06-11-pi-agent-harness-patterns-brief#2', '2026-06-11-pi-agent-harness-patterns-brief', 2, 'Summary',
  '## Summary

Pi is a strong reference for future Pritha child-agent design because it demonstrates a small, inspectable coding-agent core surrounded by explicit customization mechanisms: extensions, skills, prompt templates, packages, session branching, compaction, SDK/RPC and a TUI adapter. The most useful lesson is architectural discipline, not direct adoption of Pi as our default runtime. Pritha should preserve a minimal core for each descendant and add capabilities only through contract-selected modules with reviewed provenance and security boundaries.', '9372f85aad281418f0b530d2b72aa70d58f4ed85bfc4fe7675645266d81ed27a', 103
);
INSERT INTO chunks_fts (text, heading, document_id, chunk_id)
VALUES ('## Summary

Pi is a strong reference for future Pritha child-agent design because it demonstrates a small, inspectable coding-agent core surrounded by explicit customization mechanisms: extensions, skills, prompt templates, packages, session branching, compaction, SDK/RPC and a TUI adapter. The most useful lesson is architectural discipline, not direct adoption of Pi as our default runtime. Pritha should preserve a minimal core for each descendant and add capabilities only through contract-selected modules with reviewed provenance and security boundaries.', 'Summary', '2026-06-11-pi-agent-harness-patterns-brief', '2026-06-11-pi-agent-harness-patterns-brief#2');

INSERT INTO chunks (id, document_id, ordinal, heading, text, hash, token_count)
VALUES (
  '2026-06-11-pi-agent-harness-patterns-brief#3', '2026-06-11-pi-agent-harness-patterns-brief', 3, 'Patterns worth extracting',
  '## Patterns worth extracting', '1a6e8767e43f0ab7c850ba91bc5de8f3b60ab5a1d0cef69451779c432dd84e42', 6
);
INSERT INTO chunks_fts (text, heading, document_id, chunk_id)
VALUES ('## Patterns worth extracting', 'Patterns worth extracting', '2026-06-11-pi-agent-harness-patterns-brief', '2026-06-11-pi-agent-harness-patterns-brief#3');

INSERT INTO chunks (id, document_id, ordinal, heading, text, hash, token_count)
VALUES (
  '2026-06-11-pi-agent-harness-patterns-brief#4', '2026-06-11-pi-agent-harness-patterns-brief', 4, '1. Layer the agent stack',
  '### 1. Layer the agent stack

Pi separates provider API normalization, core agent loop/state, coding-agent session/resources and terminal UI. Pritha should mirror this conceptually: runtime, memory, tools, interface and operations are separate modules selected by the contract, not one inseparable bundle.', '8f5a69dd94719ce3e7bd4c5f3190c0f69266b5f925c8341d0545b9bcfc20e3c8', 56
);
INSERT INTO chunks_fts (text, heading, document_id, chunk_id)
VALUES ('### 1. Layer the agent stack

Pi separates provider API normalization, core agent loop/state, coding-agent session/resources and terminal UI. Pritha should mirror this conceptually: runtime, memory, tools, interface and operations are separate modules selected by the contract, not one inseparable bundle.', '1. Layer the agent stack', '2026-06-11-pi-agent-harness-patterns-brief', '2026-06-11-pi-agent-harness-patterns-brief#4');

INSERT INTO chunks (id, document_id, ordinal, heading, text, hash, token_count)
VALUES (
  '2026-06-11-pi-agent-harness-patterns-brief#5', '2026-06-11-pi-agent-harness-patterns-brief', 5, '2. Keep the default tool surface narrow',
  '### 2. Keep the default tool surface narrow

Pi starts from a small coding tool set and lets additional capabilities come through skills or extensions. This reinforces Techscope''s existing rule: choose CLI/script, skill, MCP, browser or manual boundary deliberately, and prefer progressive discovery over eager tool loading.', '25818b1eab104c364cca1a4a67289beb85647e7fafc67830911c66d17f95bc62', 64
);
INSERT INTO chunks_fts (text, heading, document_id, chunk_id)
VALUES ('### 2. Keep the default tool surface narrow

Pi starts from a small coding tool set and lets additional capabilities come through skills or extensions. This reinforces Techscope''s existing rule: choose CLI/script, skill, MCP, browser or manual boundary deliberately, and prefer progressive discovery over eager tool loading.', '2. Keep the default tool surface narrow', '2026-06-11-pi-agent-harness-patterns-brief', '2026-06-11-pi-agent-harness-patterns-brief#5');

INSERT INTO chunks (id, document_id, ordinal, heading, text, hash, token_count)
VALUES (
  '2026-06-11-pi-agent-harness-patterns-brief#6', '2026-06-11-pi-agent-harness-patterns-brief', 6, '3. Treat extension APIs as a real product surface',
  '### 3. Treat extension APIs as a real product surface

Extensions can register tools, commands, UI components, event handlers and persistent state. For Pritha, extensions should be described in a manifest with risk level, trust level, hooks, permissions, readiness and test cases.', 'd3e0e06e0fd628208543934f42309a9efb5563d8be4b70105e8174774c37e252', 57
);
INSERT INTO chunks_fts (text, heading, document_id, chunk_id)
VALUES ('### 3. Treat extension APIs as a real product surface

Extensions can register tools, commands, UI components, event handlers and persistent state. For Pritha, extensions should be described in a manifest with risk level, trust level, hooks, permissions, readiness and test cases.', '3. Treat extension APIs as a real product surface', '2026-06-11-pi-agent-harness-patterns-brief', '2026-06-11-pi-agent-harness-patterns-brief#6');

INSERT INTO chunks (id, document_id, ordinal, heading, text, hash, token_count)
VALUES (
  '2026-06-11-pi-agent-harness-patterns-brief#7', '2026-06-11-pi-agent-harness-patterns-brief', 7, '4. Store sessions as structured state, not only chat text',
  '### 4. Store sessions as structured state, not only chat text

Pi''s session format supports model messages, tool results, model changes, thinking-level changes, custom extension state, compaction and branch summaries. Future agents should not flatten all durable state into transcript prose; structured entries are easier to inspect, migrate, summarize and replay.', 'a7881f8a93592e38b9d3f4e2b739f80517c933968a7a4a7b784dcfaedc05bf09', 69
);
INSERT INTO chunks_fts (text, heading, document_id, chunk_id)
VALUES ('### 4. Store sessions as structured state, not only chat text

Pi''s session format supports model messages, tool results, model changes, thinking-level changes, custom extension state, compaction and branch summaries. Future agents should not flatten all durable state into transcript prose; structured entries are easier to inspect, migrate, summarize and replay.', '4. Store sessions as structured state, not only chat text', '2026-06-11-pi-agent-harness-patterns-brief', '2026-06-11-pi-agent-harness-patterns-brief#7');

INSERT INTO chunks (id, document_id, ordinal, heading, text, hash, token_count)
VALUES (
  '2026-06-11-pi-agent-harness-patterns-brief#8', '2026-06-11-pi-agent-harness-patterns-brief', 8, '5. Use session trees for side quests',
  '### 5. Use session trees for side quests

Branching allows a repair, review or experiment to happen without poisoning the main path. This is relevant for Pritha-created coding agents: a review branch can inspect work and return summarized findings to the main branch.', 'efac075ddb7afe0793dda6076677d41fb8c3758810e92ee031d6c80b4eca3698', 59
);
INSERT INTO chunks_fts (text, heading, document_id, chunk_id)
VALUES ('### 5. Use session trees for side quests

Branching allows a repair, review or experiment to happen without poisoning the main path. This is relevant for Pritha-created coding agents: a review branch can inspect work and return summarized findings to the main branch.', '5. Use session trees for side quests', '2026-06-11-pi-agent-harness-patterns-brief', '2026-06-11-pi-agent-harness-patterns-brief#8');

INSERT INTO chunks (id, document_id, ordinal, heading, text, hash, token_count)
VALUES (
  '2026-06-11-pi-agent-harness-patterns-brief#9', '2026-06-11-pi-agent-harness-patterns-brief', 9, '6. Make compaction structured and file-aware',
  '### 6. Make compaction structured and file-aware

Pi compaction keeps a summary plus the boundary of retained messages and tracks read/modified files. Pritha should require compaction/handoff summaries to preserve goal, constraints, progress, blockers, decisions, next steps and touched files.', 'fd3370856e0fabfa49a2adec2cecad2dc5827f06e652a6cabbf1c977cb4fbda6', 53
);
INSERT INTO chunks_fts (text, heading, document_id, chunk_id)
VALUES ('### 6. Make compaction structured and file-aware

Pi compaction keeps a summary plus the boundary of retained messages and tracks read/modified files. Pritha should require compaction/handoff summaries to preserve goal, constraints, progress, blockers, decisions, next steps and touched files.', '6. Make compaction structured and file-aware', '2026-06-11-pi-agent-harness-patterns-brief', '2026-06-11-pi-agent-harness-patterns-brief#9');

INSERT INTO chunks (id, document_id, ordinal, heading, text, hash, token_count)
VALUES (
  '2026-06-11-pi-agent-harness-patterns-brief#10', '2026-06-11-pi-agent-harness-patterns-brief', 10, '7. Separate UI from runtime',
  '### 7. Separate UI from runtime

Pi supports interactive TUI, print/JSON, RPC and SDK embedding. Pritha should treat Telegram, web UI, voice, CLI and Codex thread as adapters around a task/session runtime when the agent''s scope justifies that separation.', '720c1cedd0539854e31eab3c122a73ae7bb79e11890263e07869ea3cda1d0bf7', 53
);
INSERT INTO chunks_fts (text, heading, document_id, chunk_id)
VALUES ('### 7. Separate UI from runtime

Pi supports interactive TUI, print/JSON, RPC and SDK embedding. Pritha should treat Telegram, web UI, voice, CLI and Codex thread as adapters around a task/session runtime when the agent''s scope justifies that separation.', '7. Separate UI from runtime', '2026-06-11-pi-agent-harness-patterns-brief', '2026-06-11-pi-agent-harness-patterns-brief#10');

INSERT INTO chunks (id, document_id, ordinal, heading, text, hash, token_count)
VALUES (
  '2026-06-11-pi-agent-harness-patterns-brief#11', '2026-06-11-pi-agent-harness-patterns-brief', 11, '8. Trust gates are not sandboxes',
  '### 8. Trust gates are not sandboxes

Pi''s project trust is useful for deciding whether to load project-local resources, but Pi explicitly says it is not a security boundary. Pritha should keep this distinction: project trust, package approval and runtime isolation are separate contract fields.', '9ac09cb86ba65da786c907be8d6646570634f888d8117ed3becf52b11c8722fb', 61
);
INSERT INTO chunks_fts (text, heading, document_id, chunk_id)
VALUES ('### 8. Trust gates are not sandboxes

Pi''s project trust is useful for deciding whether to load project-local resources, but Pi explicitly says it is not a security boundary. Pritha should keep this distinction: project trust, package approval and runtime isolation are separate contract fields.', '8. Trust gates are not sandboxes', '2026-06-11-pi-agent-harness-patterns-brief', '2026-06-11-pi-agent-harness-patterns-brief#11');

INSERT INTO chunks (id, document_id, ordinal, heading, text, hash, token_count)
VALUES (
  '2026-06-11-pi-agent-harness-patterns-brief#12', '2026-06-11-pi-agent-harness-patterns-brief', 12, '9. Packageability is useful only with supply-chain discipline',
  '### 9. Packageability is useful only with supply-chain discipline

Bundling extensions, skills, prompts and themes as packages is powerful, but package installs execute code and can change agent behavior. External packages should remain candidate-only until pinned, reviewed and eval-covered.', '858fcd7cfa2cdb07d42ce1f4dc2650f6f0bee4a1051998dce7885fdda7e1f667', 53
);
INSERT INTO chunks_fts (text, heading, document_id, chunk_id)
VALUES ('### 9. Packageability is useful only with supply-chain discipline

Bundling extensions, skills, prompts and themes as packages is powerful, but package installs execute code and can change agent behavior. External packages should remain candidate-only until pinned, reviewed and eval-covered.', '9. Packageability is useful only with supply-chain discipline', '2026-06-11-pi-agent-harness-patterns-brief', '2026-06-11-pi-agent-harness-patterns-brief#12');

INSERT INTO chunks (id, document_id, ordinal, heading, text, hash, token_count)
VALUES (
  '2026-06-11-pi-agent-harness-patterns-brief#13', '2026-06-11-pi-agent-harness-patterns-brief', 13, '10. Self-extension is productive but high-risk',
  '### 10. Self-extension is productive but high-risk

Pi can help write its own extensions. This is a good development loop for trusted local work, but future agents should not self-enable new tools, permissions or packages in production without human approval and a recorded readiness check.', 'a94dee77b9fc4932dff773549467953cf1b83b786aaab478a183b5446111ab98', 61
);
INSERT INTO chunks_fts (text, heading, document_id, chunk_id)
VALUES ('### 10. Self-extension is productive but high-risk

Pi can help write its own extensions. This is a good development loop for trusted local work, but future agents should not self-enable new tools, permissions or packages in production without human approval and a recorded readiness check.', '10. Self-extension is productive but high-risk', '2026-06-11-pi-agent-harness-patterns-brief', '2026-06-11-pi-agent-harness-patterns-brief#13');

INSERT INTO chunks (id, document_id, ordinal, heading, text, hash, token_count)
VALUES (
  '2026-06-11-pi-agent-harness-patterns-brief#14', '2026-06-11-pi-agent-harness-patterns-brief', 14, 'Relationship to existing Techscope knowledge',
  '## Relationship to existing Techscope knowledge

- Confirms `agent-creation-harness`: child agents should be assembled from selected modules rather than cloned from one universal bundle.
- Refines `agent-tool-integration-selection`: Pi provides a concrete case for "primitives before features" and skills/CLI before broad MCP when that fits the task.
- Refines `agent-skill-pack-lifecycle`: skills are procedural memory with progressive disclosure, but still require provenance and trigger evals.
- Refines `agent-interface-experience`: UI is a harness boundary. The same runtime can support TUI, SDK, RPC or other adapters.
- Confirms `agent-untrusted-input-security`: project trust and extension loading must be separated from sandboxing and external-input policy.
- Confirms `agent-harness-evaluation`: before choosing Pi as runtime, test it against the actual agent workload.', '5b5c6d343be52cdfab8d3ae2fc00dcb24ecd3836350f43d8e1cf0a8a13395555', 153
);
INSERT INTO chunks_fts (text, heading, document_id, chunk_id)
VALUES ('## Relationship to existing Techscope knowledge

- Confirms `agent-creation-harness`: child agents should be assembled from selected modules rather than cloned from one universal bundle.
- Refines `agent-tool-integration-selection`: Pi provides a concrete case for "primitives before features" and skills/CLI before broad MCP when that fits the task.
- Refines `agent-skill-pack-lifecycle`: skills are procedural memory with progressive disclosure, but still require provenance and trigger evals.
- Refines `agent-interface-experience`: UI is a harness boundary. The same runtime can support TUI, SDK, RPC or other adapters.
- Confirms `agent-untrusted-input-security`: project trust and extension loading must be separated from sandboxing and external-input policy.
- Confirms `agent-harness-evaluation`: before choosing Pi as runtime, test it against the actual agent workload.', 'Relationship to existing Techscope knowledge', '2026-06-11-pi-agent-harness-patterns-brief', '2026-06-11-pi-agent-harness-patterns-brief#14');

INSERT INTO chunks (id, document_id, ordinal, heading, text, hash, token_count)
VALUES (
  '2026-06-11-pi-agent-harness-patterns-brief#15', '2026-06-11-pi-agent-harness-patterns-brief', 15, 'Recommendation',
  '## Recommendation

Promote the reusable design rule into `04_standards/agent-minimal-core-extension-surface.md`. Do not select Pi as Pritha''s default runtime. Treat Pi as an architecture reference and candidate runtime for future child agents only after task-specific evaluation.', 'd3208a5ed9f790336fa507bafe27b8e13ae0d5311b62975c05793c3f86c4073c', 46
);
