INSERT INTO chunks (id, document_id, ordinal, heading, text, hash, token_count)
VALUES (
  '2026-05-17-hermes-agent-architecture-assessment#2', '2026-05-17-hermes-agent-architecture-assessment', 2, 'One-paragraph read',
  '## One-paragraph read

Hermes Agent is a high-priority autonomous-agent architecture to study. It combines several patterns Techscope already cares about: long-running operation, messaging gateway, bounded memory, session search, procedural skills, toolset narrowing, MCP, subagents, cron, terminal backends, context files and security approval layers. The strongest immediate value is not installing it as our main environment, but extracting its architecture patterns and running a contained experiment.', 'd7890c107ee4eb9102a61087c5108a413cc708e549c75261bfc7dcd7d6ac0127', 88
);
INSERT INTO chunks_fts (text, heading, document_id, chunk_id)
VALUES ('## One-paragraph read

Hermes Agent is a high-priority autonomous-agent architecture to study. It combines several patterns Techscope already cares about: long-running operation, messaging gateway, bounded memory, session search, procedural skills, toolset narrowing, MCP, subagents, cron, terminal backends, context files and security approval layers. The strongest immediate value is not installing it as our main environment, but extracting its architecture patterns and running a contained experiment.', 'One-paragraph read', '2026-05-17-hermes-agent-architecture-assessment', '2026-05-17-hermes-agent-architecture-assessment#2');

INSERT INTO chunks (id, document_id, ordinal, heading, text, hash, token_count)
VALUES (
  '2026-05-17-hermes-agent-architecture-assessment#3', '2026-05-17-hermes-agent-architecture-assessment', 3, 'Why it matters',
  '## Why it matters

Hermes overlaps directly with Techscope''s mission: ingest information, remember what matters, operate through messaging interfaces, run local/server-side workflows, use tools safely and improve procedures over time. It also gives us a second major autonomous-agent reference alongside OpenClaw, which lets us distinguish recurring architecture patterns from one project''s idiosyncrasies.', 'f90f7ae8c71447b3ba524b25cfc0830274d91ac7c3f7d00482bea3c9245a2e3c', 71
);
INSERT INTO chunks_fts (text, heading, document_id, chunk_id)
VALUES ('## Why it matters

Hermes overlaps directly with Techscope''s mission: ingest information, remember what matters, operate through messaging interfaces, run local/server-side workflows, use tools safely and improve procedures over time. It also gives us a second major autonomous-agent reference alongside OpenClaw, which lets us distinguish recurring architecture patterns from one project''s idiosyncrasies.', 'Why it matters', '2026-05-17-hermes-agent-architecture-assessment', '2026-05-17-hermes-agent-architecture-assessment#3');

INSERT INTO chunks (id, document_id, ordinal, heading, text, hash, token_count)
VALUES (
  '2026-05-17-hermes-agent-architecture-assessment#4', '2026-05-17-hermes-agent-architecture-assessment', 4, 'Technical claims',
  '## Technical claims

- Long-running autonomous agents need multiple surfaces: CLI, messaging gateway, cron, API/IDE, and background workers.
- Persistent memory should be bounded and curated, while session history should remain searchable on demand.
- Procedural knowledge should be compiled into skills, not only retrieved from raw chat history.
- Tool availability must be scoped through toolsets by platform/session/task.
- Context files should be discovered progressively and scanned for injection.
- Gateway agents need explicit authorization, command approval and safe terminal backends.
- Model/provider abstraction is valuable, but every provider/runtime has different tool and auth semantics.', '2bf573c6083fab1ce62689b66b4ae475443543e2e73b5acfef401796786f4c61', 130
);
INSERT INTO chunks_fts (text, heading, document_id, chunk_id)
VALUES ('## Technical claims

- Long-running autonomous agents need multiple surfaces: CLI, messaging gateway, cron, API/IDE, and background workers.
- Persistent memory should be bounded and curated, while session history should remain searchable on demand.
- Procedural knowledge should be compiled into skills, not only retrieved from raw chat history.
- Tool availability must be scoped through toolsets by platform/session/task.
- Context files should be discovered progressively and scanned for injection.
- Gateway agents need explicit authorization, command approval and safe terminal backends.
- Model/provider abstraction is valuable, but every provider/runtime has different tool and auth semantics.', 'Technical claims', '2026-05-17-hermes-agent-architecture-assessment', '2026-05-17-hermes-agent-architecture-assessment#4');

INSERT INTO chunks (id, document_id, ordinal, heading, text, hash, token_count)
VALUES (
  '2026-05-17-hermes-agent-architecture-assessment#5', '2026-05-17-hermes-agent-architecture-assessment', 5, 'Agent environment profile',
  '## Agent environment profile

- Agent platforms: Hermes Agent, Codex as adaptation target.
- Model context: model-agnostic Hermes providers plus Codex/Codex CLI as a possible downstream runtime.
- Runtime environment: CLI, messaging gateway, VPS/cloud, Docker/SSH/Modal/Daytona/Vercel Sandbox, ACP/IDE, cron.
- Config surfaces: `config.yaml`, `AGENTS.md`, `.hermes.md`, `HERMES.md`, `CLAUDE.md`, `SOUL.md`, `.cursorrules`, skills, toolsets, MCP, plugins, memory providers.
- Portability: adapter-needed.
- Codex adaptation:
  - Keep Techscope source of truth in Markdown/SQLite/embeddings, not Hermes memory files.
  - Borrow bounded memory, procedural skills and toolset narrowing as design patterns.
  - Treat Hermes as a possible external agent runtime or comparison target, not as a replacement for Codex.
- Environment-specific caveats:
  - Hermes gateway, memory providers, skills hub, toolsets, cron and provider proxy behavior are Hermes-specific.
  - The OpenAI-compatible local proxy could affect Codex workflows, but needs security and reliability testing.', 'c36ad43883d98e4be51ddd55549c521fa592509c01cd33d2120edc30b9f139e1', 183
);
INSERT INTO chunks_fts (text, heading, document_id, chunk_id)
VALUES ('## Agent environment profile

- Agent platforms: Hermes Agent, Codex as adaptation target.
- Model context: model-agnostic Hermes providers plus Codex/Codex CLI as a possible downstream runtime.
- Runtime environment: CLI, messaging gateway, VPS/cloud, Docker/SSH/Modal/Daytona/Vercel Sandbox, ACP/IDE, cron.
- Config surfaces: `config.yaml`, `AGENTS.md`, `.hermes.md`, `HERMES.md`, `CLAUDE.md`, `SOUL.md`, `.cursorrules`, skills, toolsets, MCP, plugins, memory providers.
- Portability: adapter-needed.
- Codex adaptation:
  - Keep Techscope source of truth in Markdown/SQLite/embeddings, not Hermes memory files.
  - Borrow bounded memory, procedural skills and toolset narrowing as design patterns.
  - Treat Hermes as a possible external agent runtime or comparison target, not as a replacement for Codex.
- Environment-specific caveats:
  - Hermes gateway, memory providers, skills hub, toolsets, cron and provider proxy behavior are Hermes-specific.
  - The OpenAI-compatible local proxy could affect Codex workflows, but needs security and reliability testing.', 'Agent environment profile', '2026-05-17-hermes-agent-architecture-assessment', '2026-05-17-hermes-agent-architecture-assessment#5');

