INSERT INTO chunks (id, document_id, ordinal, heading, text, hash, token_count)
VALUES (
  '2026-05-18-techscope-agents-mother-scenario-review#2', '2026-05-18-techscope-agents-mother-scenario-review', 2, 'Question',
  '## Question

How should Techscope create new agents from user goals and technical specifications while preserving harness quality, source verification, safety and reproducibility?', '550f647ebe2899257f314ccb883da6591772cacd2aa0834e24225017ecb78cc5', 32
);
INSERT INTO chunks_fts (text, heading, document_id, chunk_id)
VALUES ('## Question

How should Techscope create new agents from user goals and technical specifications while preserving harness quality, source verification, safety and reproducibility?', 'Question', '2026-05-18-techscope-agents-mother-scenario-review', '2026-05-18-techscope-agents-mother-scenario-review#2');

INSERT INTO chunks (id, document_id, ordinal, heading, text, hash, token_count)
VALUES (
  '2026-05-18-techscope-agents-mother-scenario-review#3', '2026-05-18-techscope-agents-mother-scenario-review', 3, 'Proposed scenario',
  '## Proposed scenario

`Techscope - Agents Mother` is a new scenario where Techscope becomes an agent factory:

- elicit or accept a target-agent specification;
- research relevant architectures and tools from Techscope memory plus current official/web sources;
- choose a runtime/shell pattern;
- scaffold a sibling project folder;
- write agent instructions, workflows, tools, validation and onboarding docs;
- test the result;
- train the user to operate the new agent.', 'dc215c8de108ce8f63b7d919657e2fa90fbdd78912b1e2050b50b3e5d53f9d4e', 96
);
INSERT INTO chunks_fts (text, heading, document_id, chunk_id)
VALUES ('## Proposed scenario

`Techscope - Agents Mother` is a new scenario where Techscope becomes an agent factory:

- elicit or accept a target-agent specification;
- research relevant architectures and tools from Techscope memory plus current official/web sources;
- choose a runtime/shell pattern;
- scaffold a sibling project folder;
- write agent instructions, workflows, tools, validation and onboarding docs;
- test the result;
- train the user to operate the new agent.', 'Proposed scenario', '2026-05-18-techscope-agents-mother-scenario-review', '2026-05-18-techscope-agents-mother-scenario-review#3');

INSERT INTO chunks (id, document_id, ordinal, heading, text, hash, token_count)
VALUES (
  '2026-05-18-techscope-agents-mother-scenario-review#4', '2026-05-18-techscope-agents-mother-scenario-review', 4, 'Runtime options',
  '## Runtime options

| Option | Fit | Notes |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Codex project agent | Best default for coding/project agents | Uses sibling folder, `AGENTS.md`, scripts, tests, local files |
| Codex CLI wrapper | Good for terminal-first repeatable agent | Needs CLI commands, config, permissions, logs |
| API-based agent | Good for productized app/bot | Needs OpenAI Agents SDK or similar orchestration, state, guardrails |
| Local-model agent | Good for privacy/offline constraints | Needs inference stack, evals, model limits, hardware check |
| Hybrid Telegram/web agent | Good for non-coder workflows | Needs queue, concise responses, allowlist, media pipeline |', '66385b0082a5c4258f33e0550284afb5f196fce69bba2f2f74e623707bcbad53', 149
);
INSERT INTO chunks_fts (text, heading, document_id, chunk_id)
VALUES ('## Runtime options

| Option | Fit | Notes |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Codex project agent | Best default for coding/project agents | Uses sibling folder, `AGENTS.md`, scripts, tests, local files |
| Codex CLI wrapper | Good for terminal-first repeatable agent | Needs CLI commands, config, permissions, logs |
| API-based agent | Good for productized app/bot | Needs OpenAI Agents SDK or similar orchestration, state, guardrails |
| Local-model agent | Good for privacy/offline constraints | Needs inference stack, evals, model limits, hardware check |
| Hybrid Telegram/web agent | Good for non-coder workflows | Needs queue, concise responses, allowlist, media pipeline |', 'Runtime options', '2026-05-18-techscope-agents-mother-scenario-review', '2026-05-18-techscope-agents-mother-scenario-review#4');

INSERT INTO chunks (id, document_id, ordinal, heading, text, hash, token_count)
VALUES (
  '2026-05-18-techscope-agents-mother-scenario-review#5', '2026-05-18-techscope-agents-mother-scenario-review', 5, 'Harness requirements',
  '## Harness requirements

Use six harness layers:

1. Information boundaries: role, mission, source of truth, output contracts.
2. Tool system: tools, when to use them, filtered outputs, permissions.
3. Execution orchestration: workflow states, queues, routing, handoff rules.
4. Memory and state: short-term task state, long-term memory, generated wiki if useful.
5. Evaluation and observability: tests, lint, logs, traces, screenshots, metrics.
6. Constraints, validation and recovery: guardrails, retry/fallback, rollback, human approval.', '5a2dbe816b773e41861edef9227d0baea32e0047ed61e699778cad8254e39aed', 95
);
INSERT INTO chunks_fts (text, heading, document_id, chunk_id)
VALUES ('## Harness requirements

Use six harness layers:

1. Information boundaries: role, mission, source of truth, output contracts.
2. Tool system: tools, when to use them, filtered outputs, permissions.
3. Execution orchestration: workflow states, queues, routing, handoff rules.
4. Memory and state: short-term task state, long-term memory, generated wiki if useful.
5. Evaluation and observability: tests, lint, logs, traces, screenshots, metrics.
6. Constraints, validation and recovery: guardrails, retry/fallback, rollback, human approval.', 'Harness requirements', '2026-05-18-techscope-agents-mother-scenario-review', '2026-05-18-techscope-agents-mother-scenario-review#5');

INSERT INTO chunks (id, document_id, ordinal, heading, text, hash, token_count)
VALUES (
  '2026-05-18-techscope-agents-mother-scenario-review#6', '2026-05-18-techscope-agents-mother-scenario-review', 6, 'Evidence from current validation',
  '## Evidence from current validation

- OpenAI Agents SDK docs separate direct API clients from SDK-owned orchestration, tools, approvals and state.
- OpenAI agent guide recommends starting with a single agent and moving to multi-agent only when tool/instruction complexity requires it.
- OpenAI guardrails docs distinguish input, output and tool guardrails; tool guardrails matter for every function call.
- OpenAI Codex repo describes Codex CLI as a local coding agent, suitable as a project/sibling-folder baseline.
- Anthropic recommends simple composable workflows, focused tools and clear success criteria; coding agents are especially suitable because tests provide feedback.
- Anthropic context engineering guidance supports tight context, minimal viable tool sets, just-in-time retrieval, compaction, notes and subagents.
- LangGraph production-agent guidance emphasizes durable execution, checkpointing, retries, human-in-the-loop and separate short/long-term memory.', '684119ee4a55b3203c718e9ddb3edf7b62304e2297aa553fa45224d913c39a6a', 173
);
INSERT INTO chunks_fts (text, heading, document_id, chunk_id)
VALUES ('## Evidence from current validation

- OpenAI Agents SDK docs separate direct API clients from SDK-owned orchestration, tools, approvals and state.
- OpenAI agent guide recommends starting with a single agent and moving to multi-agent only when tool/instruction complexity requires it.
- OpenAI guardrails docs distinguish input, output and tool guardrails; tool guardrails matter for every function call.
- OpenAI Codex repo describes Codex CLI as a local coding agent, suitable as a project/sibling-folder baseline.
- Anthropic recommends simple composable workflows, focused tools and clear success criteria; coding agents are especially suitable because tests provide feedback.
- Anthropic context engineering guidance supports tight context, minimal viable tool sets, just-in-time retrieval, compaction, notes and subagents.
- LangGraph production-agent guidance emphasizes durable execution, checkpointing, retries, human-in-the-loop and separate short/long-term memory.', 'Evidence from current validation', '2026-05-18-techscope-agents-mother-scenario-review', '2026-05-18-techscope-agents-mother-scenario-review#6');

INSERT INTO chunks (id, document_id, ordinal, heading, text, hash, token_count)
VALUES (
  '2026-05-18-techscope-agents-mother-scenario-review#7', '2026-05-18-techscope-agents-mother-scenario-review', 7, 'Risks',
  '## Risks

- Copying Techscope 1:1 creates overbuilt agents for simple tasks.
- Asking too few questions creates vague agents with no verification.
- Asking too many questions blocks momentum.
- API/local-model agents have security, cost and deployment complexity not present in a Codex-project agent.
- Generated agent instructions can drift unless tests and maintenance docs are created.', '1daccbab3c4e1a9bdf25b85cf9598553a07e222c6dc1ec288752bf4acb2cd6fe', 79
);
INSERT INTO chunks_fts (text, heading, document_id, chunk_id)
VALUES ('## Risks

- Copying Techscope 1:1 creates overbuilt agents for simple tasks.
- Asking too few questions creates vague agents with no verification.
- Asking too many questions blocks momentum.
- API/local-model agents have security, cost and deployment complexity not present in a Codex-project agent.
- Generated agent instructions can drift unless tests and maintenance docs are created.', 'Risks', '2026-05-18-techscope-agents-mother-scenario-review', '2026-05-18-techscope-agents-mother-scenario-review#7');

INSERT INTO chunks (id, document_id, ordinal, heading, text, hash, token_count)
VALUES (
  '2026-05-18-techscope-agents-mother-scenario-review#8', '2026-05-18-techscope-agents-mother-scenario-review', 8, 'Recommendation',
  '## Recommendation

Create `Agents Mother` as a workflow and script-assisted scaffold, not as a fully autonomous black box.

Default path:

1. Intake/spec interview.
2. Agent-shell evaluation.
3. Harness design.
4. Sibling folder scaffold.
5. Validation and smoke tests.
6. User onboarding.
7. Memory registration in Techscope.', '767fcc968a75af95e43d4d3a585367c289a35105b320f1ff243028b7e0f5d7ff', 63
);
INSERT INTO chunks_fts (text, heading, document_id, chunk_id)
VALUES ('## Recommendation

Create `Agents Mother` as a workflow and script-assisted scaffold, not as a fully autonomous black box.

Default path:

1. Intake/spec interview.
2. Agent-shell evaluation.
3. Harness design.
4. Sibling folder scaffold.
5. Validation and smoke tests.
6. User onboarding.
7. Memory registration in Techscope.', 'Recommendation', '2026-05-18-techscope-agents-mother-scenario-review', '2026-05-18-techscope-agents-mother-scenario-review#8');

INSERT INTO chunks (id, document_id, ordinal, heading, text, hash, token_count)
VALUES (
  '2026-05-18-techscope-agents-mother-scenario-review#9', '2026-05-18-techscope-agents-mother-scenario-review', 9, 'Open questions',
  '## Open questions

- Should v1 generate only Codex-project agents, or support API/CLI/local model branches immediately?
- What should be the canonical sibling folder root?
- Should created agents get their own Obsidian/Markdown memory by default?
- Do we want a reusable `scripts/create-agent.mjs` scaffold generator in Techscope?
- Should every created agent be registered in a Techscope index/catalog?', '2ddcb1005a7a2ea973359be24c99c96dd7d0d05a96a165462144a71587eb4bfc', 79
);
INSERT INTO chunks_fts (text, heading, document_id, chunk_id)
VALUES ('## Open questions

- Should v1 generate only Codex-project agents, or support API/CLI/local model branches immediately?
- What should be the canonical sibling folder root?
- Should created agents get their own Obsidian/Markdown memory by default?
- Do we want a reusable `scripts/create-agent.mjs` scaffold generator in Techscope?
- Should every created agent be registered in a Techscope index/catalog?', 'Open questions', '2026-05-18-techscope-agents-mother-scenario-review', '2026-05-18-techscope-agents-mother-scenario-review#9');

