VALUES ('# Assessment: NVIDIA NemoClaw sandboxed agent runtime

Date: 2026-05-27
Status: draft
Recommendation: review', 'Assessment: NVIDIA NemoClaw sandboxed agent runtime', 'assessment-nvidia-nemoclaw-sandboxed-agent-runtime-2026-05-27', 'assessment-nvidia-nemoclaw-sandboxed-agent-runtime-2026-05-27#1');

INSERT INTO chunks (id, document_id, ordinal, heading, text, hash, token_count)
VALUES (
  'assessment-nvidia-nemoclaw-sandboxed-agent-runtime-2026-05-27#2', 'assessment-nvidia-nemoclaw-sandboxed-agent-runtime-2026-05-27', 2, 'One-paragraph read',
  '## One-paragraph read

NemoClaw is NVIDIA''s alpha reference stack for running OpenClaw inside OpenShell with sandboxing, policy-controlled network access, routed inference, messaging-channel setup and host-side credential handling. The durable value for Techscope is not "use NemoClaw everywhere", but the runtime-boundary pattern for always-on agents that ingest external messages, use integrations and may act autonomously.', 'bc8f2cdf8264c07ae826c414cc68f7e3e3f3a31070bac6483af1676ee882f11f', 73
);
INSERT INTO chunks_fts (text, heading, document_id, chunk_id)
VALUES ('## One-paragraph read

NemoClaw is NVIDIA''s alpha reference stack for running OpenClaw inside OpenShell with sandboxing, policy-controlled network access, routed inference, messaging-channel setup and host-side credential handling. The durable value for Techscope is not "use NemoClaw everywhere", but the runtime-boundary pattern for always-on agents that ingest external messages, use integrations and may act autonomously.', 'One-paragraph read', 'assessment-nvidia-nemoclaw-sandboxed-agent-runtime-2026-05-27', 'assessment-nvidia-nemoclaw-sandboxed-agent-runtime-2026-05-27#2');

INSERT INTO chunks (id, document_id, ordinal, heading, text, hash, token_count)
VALUES (
  'assessment-nvidia-nemoclaw-sandboxed-agent-runtime-2026-05-27#3', 'assessment-nvidia-nemoclaw-sandboxed-agent-runtime-2026-05-27', 3, 'Why it matters',
  '## Why it matters

Agents Mother is moving from local scaffolds to real agents with web UIs, voice, Telegram, queues, launchd services, media ingestion and external verification. NemoClaw shows a concrete version of the harness layer we need to ask about before creating a powerful agent: where does the agent run, who owns credentials, how is network egress approved, how are integrations scoped, and how can a sandbox be recreated from a versioned blueprint?', 'f008c9c12e4375675f78234262967f991b8c8ed16becf9c769652917a8b3c147', 100
);
INSERT INTO chunks_fts (text, heading, document_id, chunk_id)
VALUES ('## Why it matters

Agents Mother is moving from local scaffolds to real agents with web UIs, voice, Telegram, queues, launchd services, media ingestion and external verification. NemoClaw shows a concrete version of the harness layer we need to ask about before creating a powerful agent: where does the agent run, who owns credentials, how is network egress approved, how are integrations scoped, and how can a sandbox be recreated from a versioned blueprint?', 'Why it matters', 'assessment-nvidia-nemoclaw-sandboxed-agent-runtime-2026-05-27', 'assessment-nvidia-nemoclaw-sandboxed-agent-runtime-2026-05-27#3');

INSERT INTO chunks (id, document_id, ordinal, heading, text, hash, token_count)
VALUES (
  'assessment-nvidia-nemoclaw-sandboxed-agent-runtime-2026-05-27#4', 'assessment-nvidia-nemoclaw-sandboxed-agent-runtime-2026-05-27', 4, 'Technical claims',
  '## Technical claims

- OpenShell-backed sandboxing can separate host operator control from in-agent execution.
- Provider credentials should live on the host/gateway, not in the sandboxed agent.
- Inference can be routed through a local gateway address, keeping provider/model selection outside the agent.
- Network policy should be deny-by-default and integration-specific.
- Messaging channels should be configured as managed adapters with explicit policies.
- Versioned blueprints and lifecycle commands make agent runtimes more reproducible.', 'c450efd50eab70b3324077835b194b89c3308cca33be150719e93bf1543a5b0a', 100
);
INSERT INTO chunks_fts (text, heading, document_id, chunk_id)
VALUES ('## Technical claims

- OpenShell-backed sandboxing can separate host operator control from in-agent execution.
- Provider credentials should live on the host/gateway, not in the sandboxed agent.
- Inference can be routed through a local gateway address, keeping provider/model selection outside the agent.
- Network policy should be deny-by-default and integration-specific.
- Messaging channels should be configured as managed adapters with explicit policies.
- Versioned blueprints and lifecycle commands make agent runtimes more reproducible.', 'Technical claims', 'assessment-nvidia-nemoclaw-sandboxed-agent-runtime-2026-05-27', 'assessment-nvidia-nemoclaw-sandboxed-agent-runtime-2026-05-27#4');

INSERT INTO chunks (id, document_id, ordinal, heading, text, hash, token_count)
VALUES (
  'assessment-nvidia-nemoclaw-sandboxed-agent-runtime-2026-05-27#5', 'assessment-nvidia-nemoclaw-sandboxed-agent-runtime-2026-05-27', 5, 'Agent environment profile',
  '## Agent environment profile

- Agent platforms: OpenClaw and OpenShell directly; Codex through adapter pattern.
- Model context: hosted providers, local inference, routed model pools.
- Runtime environment: host CLI, OpenShell gateway, Docker sandbox, messaging adapters.
- Config surfaces: blueprints, sandbox policy YAML, router config, CLI lifecycle.
- Portability: adapter-needed.
- Codex adaptation: apply the contract questions and runtime-boundary concepts; do not copy OpenClaw-specific files into Codex projects by default.
- Environment-specific caveats: NemoClaw assumes OpenClaw/OpenShell and Docker-like runtime support.', 'eb0e5cd22c8d21a73b57355409fe4927d4d0b2caf2c6bd76994cf00b47e2ca73', 108
);
INSERT INTO chunks_fts (text, heading, document_id, chunk_id)
VALUES ('## Agent environment profile

- Agent platforms: OpenClaw and OpenShell directly; Codex through adapter pattern.
- Model context: hosted providers, local inference, routed model pools.
- Runtime environment: host CLI, OpenShell gateway, Docker sandbox, messaging adapters.
- Config surfaces: blueprints, sandbox policy YAML, router config, CLI lifecycle.
- Portability: adapter-needed.
- Codex adaptation: apply the contract questions and runtime-boundary concepts; do not copy OpenClaw-specific files into Codex projects by default.
- Environment-specific caveats: NemoClaw assumes OpenClaw/OpenShell and Docker-like runtime support.', 'Agent environment profile', 'assessment-nvidia-nemoclaw-sandboxed-agent-runtime-2026-05-27', 'assessment-nvidia-nemoclaw-sandboxed-agent-runtime-2026-05-27#5');

