INSERT INTO chunks_fts (text, heading, document_id, chunk_id)
VALUES ('# Assessment: OpenAI harness engineering for agent-readable repositories

Date: 2026-05-31
Status: draft
Recommendation: standard', 'Assessment: OpenAI harness engineering for agent-readable repositories', '2026-05-31-openai-harness-engineering-agent-readable-repo-assessment', '2026-05-31-openai-harness-engineering-agent-readable-repo-assessment#1');

INSERT INTO chunks (id, document_id, ordinal, heading, text, hash, token_count)
VALUES (
  '2026-05-31-openai-harness-engineering-agent-readable-repo-assessment#2', '2026-05-31-openai-harness-engineering-agent-readable-repo-assessment', 2, 'One-paragraph read',
  '## One-paragraph read

OpenAI''s harness-engineering article is one of the strongest primary sources for Techscope''s current direction. Its core lesson is not "agents write code now"; it is that agent productivity depends on the surrounding harness: repository-local knowledge, concise instruction maps, mechanical constraints, runnable checks, browser/observability feedback and a cleanup loop that turns repeated human judgment into durable artifacts. The material confirms our existing Pritha architecture and justifies making agent-readable repository design a stronger part of `agent-creation-harness`.', 'fe2da27d5cfc82ca84d631e270316dc1b25d7a5e24e269ecb62e35206c516d2c', 104
);
INSERT INTO chunks_fts (text, heading, document_id, chunk_id)
VALUES ('## One-paragraph read

OpenAI''s harness-engineering article is one of the strongest primary sources for Techscope''s current direction. Its core lesson is not "agents write code now"; it is that agent productivity depends on the surrounding harness: repository-local knowledge, concise instruction maps, mechanical constraints, runnable checks, browser/observability feedback and a cleanup loop that turns repeated human judgment into durable artifacts. The material confirms our existing Pritha architecture and justifies making agent-readable repository design a stronger part of `agent-creation-harness`.', 'One-paragraph read', '2026-05-31-openai-harness-engineering-agent-readable-repo-assessment', '2026-05-31-openai-harness-engineering-agent-readable-repo-assessment#2');

INSERT INTO chunks (id, document_id, ordinal, heading, text, hash, token_count)
VALUES (
  '2026-05-31-openai-harness-engineering-agent-readable-repo-assessment#3', '2026-05-31-openai-harness-engineering-agent-readable-repo-assessment', 3, 'Why it matters',
  '## Why it matters

Pritha creates descendants that must remain understandable to future Codex sessions. This source gives direct OpenAI evidence for the same design pressure: what the agent cannot find, run or verify inside the repo effectively does not exist for the agent. That maps cleanly to Techscope''s Markdown memory, standards, workflows, contracts, reports, quality gates and recent voice/FESPA/Funny Teacher lifecycle evidence.', '123892b5c5f6d17726450b71524d0804bd35ec115ebb1647e38af724412d3292', 86
);
INSERT INTO chunks_fts (text, heading, document_id, chunk_id)
VALUES ('## Why it matters

Pritha creates descendants that must remain understandable to future Codex sessions. This source gives direct OpenAI evidence for the same design pressure: what the agent cannot find, run or verify inside the repo effectively does not exist for the agent. That maps cleanly to Techscope''s Markdown memory, standards, workflows, contracts, reports, quality gates and recent voice/FESPA/Funny Teacher lifecycle evidence.', 'Why it matters', '2026-05-31-openai-harness-engineering-agent-readable-repo-assessment', '2026-05-31-openai-harness-engineering-agent-readable-repo-assessment#3');

INSERT INTO chunks (id, document_id, ordinal, heading, text, hash, token_count)
VALUES (
  '2026-05-31-openai-harness-engineering-agent-readable-repo-assessment#4', '2026-05-31-openai-harness-engineering-agent-readable-repo-assessment', 4, 'Technical claims',
  '## Technical claims

- `AGENTS.md` should be concise and map-like; detailed knowledge belongs in structured repository docs.
- Repository-local knowledge is the durable system of record for agents.
- Browser state, UI behavior, logs, metrics and traces should be made legible to Codex where they affect correctness.
- Mechanical guardrails scale better than repeated human reminders.
- Architecture constraints should be encoded in linters, tests, dependency rules and typed boundaries where possible.
- Review feedback should become docs, checks or tools when it repeats.
- Higher autonomy is not portable by prompt alone; it requires comparable harness investment.', 'abc9ed105d3d5ae513208c202f09c4ba3dbc2fd249d3f7f5f9ab2fbc4f997598', 133
);
INSERT INTO chunks_fts (text, heading, document_id, chunk_id)
VALUES ('## Technical claims

- `AGENTS.md` should be concise and map-like; detailed knowledge belongs in structured repository docs.
- Repository-local knowledge is the durable system of record for agents.
- Browser state, UI behavior, logs, metrics and traces should be made legible to Codex where they affect correctness.
- Mechanical guardrails scale better than repeated human reminders.
- Architecture constraints should be encoded in linters, tests, dependency rules and typed boundaries where possible.
- Review feedback should become docs, checks or tools when it repeats.
- Higher autonomy is not portable by prompt alone; it requires comparable harness investment.', 'Technical claims', '2026-05-31-openai-harness-engineering-agent-readable-repo-assessment', '2026-05-31-openai-harness-engineering-agent-readable-repo-assessment#4');

INSERT INTO chunks (id, document_id, ordinal, heading, text, hash, token_count)
VALUES (
  '2026-05-31-openai-harness-engineering-agent-readable-repo-assessment#5', '2026-05-31-openai-harness-engineering-agent-readable-repo-assessment', 5, 'Agent environment profile',
  '## Agent environment profile

- Agent platforms: Codex.
- Model context: GPT-5-era Codex practice described by OpenAI.
- Runtime environment: git worktrees, local app instances, browser/DevTools, CI and observability.
- Config surfaces: `AGENTS.md`, docs, execution plans, linters, structural tests, CI, metrics/logs/traces.
- Portability: codex-native for Techscope; adapter-needed for other coding agents.
- Codex adaptation: fold the source into Pritha''s scaffold/standard layer, not as a new runtime dependency.
- Environment-specific caveats: OpenAI''s internal throughput and autonomy depend on an internal product harness and should not be expected in small projects without similar checks.', '3435783c92276423ce8352f308844935f29f42af9ac3c5e7318f1ab4b5627261', 125
);
INSERT INTO chunks_fts (text, heading, document_id, chunk_id)
VALUES ('## Agent environment profile

- Agent platforms: Codex.
- Model context: GPT-5-era Codex practice described by OpenAI.
- Runtime environment: git worktrees, local app instances, browser/DevTools, CI and observability.
- Config surfaces: `AGENTS.md`, docs, execution plans, linters, structural tests, CI, metrics/logs/traces.
- Portability: codex-native for Techscope; adapter-needed for other coding agents.
- Codex adaptation: fold the source into Pritha''s scaffold/standard layer, not as a new runtime dependency.
- Environment-specific caveats: OpenAI''s internal throughput and autonomy depend on an internal product harness and should not be expected in small projects without similar checks.', 'Agent environment profile', '2026-05-31-openai-harness-engineering-agent-readable-repo-assessment', '2026-05-31-openai-harness-engineering-agent-readable-repo-assessment#5');

