INSERT INTO chunks (id, document_id, ordinal, heading, text, hash, token_count)
VALUES (
  '2026-06-02-agentic-ui-source-batch-review#5', '2026-06-02-agentic-ui-source-batch-review', 5, 'Outcome-Oriented Interface',
  '### Outcome-Oriented Interface

When an agent acts on behalf of a user, the interface should show:

- goal and current plan;
- what the agent can do autonomously;
- what needs approval;
- progress and blockers;
- editable state;
- cancellation/pause/retry;
- final result and audit trail.', 'e52fa984f7179682845cda15c65f50b806f0994150bbd7b4741384efea0f3604', 64
);
INSERT INTO chunks_fts (text, heading, document_id, chunk_id)
VALUES ('### Outcome-Oriented Interface

When an agent acts on behalf of a user, the interface should show:

- goal and current plan;
- what the agent can do autonomously;
- what needs approval;
- progress and blockers;
- editable state;
- cancellation/pause/retry;
- final result and audit trail.', 'Outcome-Oriented Interface', '2026-06-02-agentic-ui-source-batch-review', '2026-06-02-agentic-ui-source-batch-review#5');

INSERT INTO chunks (id, document_id, ordinal, heading, text, hash, token_count)
VALUES (
  '2026-06-02-agentic-ui-source-batch-review#6', '2026-06-02-agentic-ui-source-batch-review', 6, 'Event-Stream UI',
  '### Event-Stream UI

Use an event-stream UI when frontend and backend need to synchronize:

- partial messages;
- tool call start/end/error;
- state deltas;
- lifecycle events;
- thread/run IDs;
- cancellation and concurrency;
- approval gates.', 'c95fa19cb5e14e2da41c310bde00fa8ad882fdfc8fa93286410803e293568917', 50
);
INSERT INTO chunks_fts (text, heading, document_id, chunk_id)
VALUES ('### Event-Stream UI

Use an event-stream UI when frontend and backend need to synchronize:

- partial messages;
- tool call start/end/error;
- state deltas;
- lifecycle events;
- thread/run IDs;
- cancellation and concurrency;
- approval gates.', 'Event-Stream UI', '2026-06-02-agentic-ui-source-batch-review', '2026-06-02-agentic-ui-source-batch-review#6');

INSERT INTO chunks (id, document_id, ordinal, heading, text, hash, token_count)
VALUES (
  '2026-06-02-agentic-ui-source-batch-review#7', '2026-06-02-agentic-ui-source-batch-review', 7, 'Interactive Tool Result',
  '### Interactive Tool Result

Use MCP App/MCP UI-style widgets when a tool result is too rich for text:

- product cards;
- forms and selectors;
- dashboards;
- maps;
- charts;
- approval panels;
- multi-step workflow panels.

The widget must not bypass the agent''s side-effect policy. It should express
user intent back to the host/agent, which applies permissions and approvals.', '232377bd0794affb43128d0e386d205fed40a97056ed17230a83e773b432af5f', 83
);
INSERT INTO chunks_fts (text, heading, document_id, chunk_id)
VALUES ('### Interactive Tool Result

Use MCP App/MCP UI-style widgets when a tool result is too rich for text:

- product cards;
- forms and selectors;
- dashboards;
- maps;
- charts;
- approval panels;
- multi-step workflow panels.

The widget must not bypass the agent''s side-effect policy. It should express
user intent back to the host/agent, which applies permissions and approvals.', 'Interactive Tool Result', '2026-06-02-agentic-ui-source-batch-review', '2026-06-02-agentic-ui-source-batch-review#7');

INSERT INTO chunks (id, document_id, ordinal, heading, text, hash, token_count)
VALUES (
  '2026-06-02-agentic-ui-source-batch-review#8', '2026-06-02-agentic-ui-source-batch-review', 8, 'Declarative Generated UI',
  '### Declarative Generated UI

Use A2UI-style declarative components when the host application should retain
control over:

- design system and styling;
- accessibility;
- native rendering across platforms;
- security;
- allowed component catalog;
- incremental updates.

This is especially relevant for remote or multi-agent contexts where executing
arbitrary HTML/JavaScript is too risky or visually inconsistent.', '478d25ff46a8f96b18eeb0682a4864ebbd33c03f4e56b976d0429ce0a40b25b9', 76
);
INSERT INTO chunks_fts (text, heading, document_id, chunk_id)
VALUES ('### Declarative Generated UI

Use A2UI-style declarative components when the host application should retain
control over:

- design system and styling;
- accessibility;
- native rendering across platforms;
- security;
- allowed component catalog;
- incremental updates.

This is especially relevant for remote or multi-agent contexts where executing
arbitrary HTML/JavaScript is too risky or visually inconsistent.', 'Declarative Generated UI', '2026-06-02-agentic-ui-source-batch-review', '2026-06-02-agentic-ui-source-batch-review#8');

INSERT INTO chunks (id, document_id, ordinal, heading, text, hash, token_count)
VALUES (
  '2026-06-02-agentic-ui-source-batch-review#9', '2026-06-02-agentic-ui-source-batch-review', 9, 'Techscope Adoption Check',
  '## Techscope Adoption Check

- Techscope/Agents Mother fit: adopt.
- Implementation cost: low for standards and contract fields, medium for a web
  scaffold placeholder, high for production AG-UI/A2UI/MCP Apps runtime.
- Operational complexity: medium-high if the UI controls side effects, secrets
  or external app permissions.
- Current architecture impact: add an interface experience standard; do not
  change the default `codex-native + optional adapters` path.
- Freshness/technology timing: volatile. A2UI and MCP Apps are evolving quickly;
  verify versions before implementation.
- Decision: add standard now, update child-agent contract and Pritha interview
  to capture interface needs; keep protocol selection optional.', '1b198d082ba28f11974f7d492c2617dfbe5d331a9217030a3d32e4ce9470d065', 133
);
INSERT INTO chunks_fts (text, heading, document_id, chunk_id)
VALUES ('## Techscope Adoption Check

- Techscope/Agents Mother fit: adopt.
- Implementation cost: low for standards and contract fields, medium for a web
  scaffold placeholder, high for production AG-UI/A2UI/MCP Apps runtime.
- Operational complexity: medium-high if the UI controls side effects, secrets
  or external app permissions.
- Current architecture impact: add an interface experience standard; do not
  change the default `codex-native + optional adapters` path.
- Freshness/technology timing: volatile. A2UI and MCP Apps are evolving quickly;
  verify versions before implementation.
- Decision: add standard now, update child-agent contract and Pritha interview
  to capture interface needs; keep protocol selection optional.', 'Techscope Adoption Check', '2026-06-02-agentic-ui-source-batch-review', '2026-06-02-agentic-ui-source-batch-review#9');

INSERT INTO chunks (id, document_id, ordinal, heading, text, hash, token_count)
VALUES (
  '2026-06-02-agentic-ui-source-batch-review#10', '2026-06-02-agentic-ui-source-batch-review', 10, 'Promotion Guidance',
  '## Promotion Guidance

Promote as Pritha doctrine:

- UI is a harness boundary, not decoration;
- rich UI is selected by workflow need;
- the user must see progress, state, approvals and cancellation when an agent
  acts over time;
- the host owns rendering and security boundaries;
- generated UI should use trusted component catalogs or sandboxed resources;
- widgets express intent, but side effects still go through agent policy;
- every selected UI layer needs fallback and readiness checks.

Do not promote as defaults:

- all agents get a web UI;
- all chat apps need generated UI;
- arbitrary agent-generated HTML/JS;
- direct widget-side destructive actions;
- protocol lock-in before the child-agent contract demands it.', '17f591530c72dcaf03c5a9ac4cc449ae0269147d30a9e4a94d6de6829641e475', 158
);
INSERT INTO chunks_fts (text, heading, document_id, chunk_id)
VALUES ('## Promotion Guidance

Promote as Pritha doctrine:

- UI is a harness boundary, not decoration;
- rich UI is selected by workflow need;
- the user must see progress, state, approvals and cancellation when an agent
  acts over time;
- the host owns rendering and security boundaries;
- generated UI should use trusted component catalogs or sandboxed resources;
- widgets express intent, but side effects still go through agent policy;
- every selected UI layer needs fallback and readiness checks.

Do not promote as defaults:

- all agents get a web UI;
- all chat apps need generated UI;
- arbitrary agent-generated HTML/JS;
- direct widget-side destructive actions;
- protocol lock-in before the child-agent contract demands it.', 'Promotion Guidance', '2026-06-02-agentic-ui-source-batch-review', '2026-06-02-agentic-ui-source-batch-review#10');

