INSERT INTO chunks_fts (text, heading, document_id, chunk_id)
VALUES ('## Consolidated Patterns', 'Consolidated Patterns', '2026-06-02-codex-surfaces-enterprise-deployment-source-batch-review', '2026-06-02-codex-surfaces-enterprise-deployment-source-batch-review#4');

INSERT INTO chunks (id, document_id, ordinal, heading, text, hash, token_count)
VALUES (
  '2026-06-02-codex-surfaces-enterprise-deployment-source-batch-review#5', '2026-06-02-codex-surfaces-enterprise-deployment-source-batch-review', 5, 'Codex Surface Profile',
  '### Codex Surface Profile

Pritha should decide which Codex surface, if any, a child agent uses:

- `cli-local`: local repo work, scripts, non-interactive automation.
- `app-supervised`: human supervises multiple agents, diffs, threads and
  worktrees.
- `cloud-task`: hosted parallel software tasks with logs and sandboxing.
- `ide-attached`: editor-native code review and implementation.
- `sdk-orchestrated`: Codex CLI exposed as an MCP server to another agent
  runtime.
- `workspace-agent`: shared team workflow agent with permissions and approvals.
- `bedrock-backed`: Codex/OpenAI models through AWS governance.
- `none`: child agent does not need Codex as a runtime surface.', 'a51d7295baabe5bfa8e86bd557227eacfd6c43583524654efa57b7745c46f77d', 126
);
INSERT INTO chunks_fts (text, heading, document_id, chunk_id)
VALUES ('### Codex Surface Profile

Pritha should decide which Codex surface, if any, a child agent uses:

- `cli-local`: local repo work, scripts, non-interactive automation.
- `app-supervised`: human supervises multiple agents, diffs, threads and
  worktrees.
- `cloud-task`: hosted parallel software tasks with logs and sandboxing.
- `ide-attached`: editor-native code review and implementation.
- `sdk-orchestrated`: Codex CLI exposed as an MCP server to another agent
  runtime.
- `workspace-agent`: shared team workflow agent with permissions and approvals.
- `bedrock-backed`: Codex/OpenAI models through AWS governance.
- `none`: child agent does not need Codex as a runtime surface.', 'Codex Surface Profile', '2026-06-02-codex-surfaces-enterprise-deployment-source-batch-review', '2026-06-02-codex-surfaces-enterprise-deployment-source-batch-review#5');

INSERT INTO chunks (id, document_id, ordinal, heading, text, hash, token_count)
VALUES (
  '2026-06-02-codex-surfaces-enterprise-deployment-source-batch-review#6', '2026-06-02-codex-surfaces-enterprise-deployment-source-batch-review', 6, 'Codex As MCP Worker',
  '### Codex As MCP Worker

Codex can be made available as an MCP server to an orchestrating agent. This is
useful when the parent agent owns planning, role routing and handoffs, while
Codex owns repo changes. The safe pattern requires:

- scoped working directory;
- explicit sandbox/approval policy;
- thread continuation via stable IDs;
- artifact gates between roles;
- trace capture;
- external grading or review.', 'c80f5a5f76f5775ef0fcc09171cd433c09e188dbac45f7136a77cf65e65ea3c4', 91
);
INSERT INTO chunks_fts (text, heading, document_id, chunk_id)
VALUES ('### Codex As MCP Worker

Codex can be made available as an MCP server to an orchestrating agent. This is
useful when the parent agent owns planning, role routing and handoffs, while
Codex owns repo changes. The safe pattern requires:

- scoped working directory;
- explicit sandbox/approval policy;
- thread continuation via stable IDs;
- artifact gates between roles;
- trace capture;
- external grading or review.', 'Codex As MCP Worker', '2026-06-02-codex-surfaces-enterprise-deployment-source-batch-review', '2026-06-02-codex-surfaces-enterprise-deployment-source-batch-review#6');

INSERT INTO chunks (id, document_id, ordinal, heading, text, hash, token_count)
VALUES (
  '2026-06-02-codex-surfaces-enterprise-deployment-source-batch-review#7', '2026-06-02-codex-surfaces-enterprise-deployment-source-batch-review', 7, 'MCP Gateway Caution',
  '### MCP Gateway Caution

Docker MCP Toolkit and similar gateways reduce setup friction for MCP servers,
credential handling and cross-platform configuration. The risk is tool-surface
inflation. Pritha should treat a gateway as an infrastructure helper, not a
trust decision. The contract still needs allowed servers, allowed tools,
credential scopes, network scope, approval modes, update policy and audit
surface.', '2f0a3bca3d920a8991fe7a12aec70aec4f6bc51d079712de0231c8f57a4d7605', 79
);
INSERT INTO chunks_fts (text, heading, document_id, chunk_id)
VALUES ('### MCP Gateway Caution

Docker MCP Toolkit and similar gateways reduce setup friction for MCP servers,
credential handling and cross-platform configuration. The risk is tool-surface
inflation. Pritha should treat a gateway as an infrastructure helper, not a
trust decision. The contract still needs allowed servers, allowed tools,
credential scopes, network scope, approval modes, update policy and audit
surface.', 'MCP Gateway Caution', '2026-06-02-codex-surfaces-enterprise-deployment-source-batch-review', '2026-06-02-codex-surfaces-enterprise-deployment-source-batch-review#7');

INSERT INTO chunks (id, document_id, ordinal, heading, text, hash, token_count)
VALUES (
  '2026-06-02-codex-surfaces-enterprise-deployment-source-batch-review#8', '2026-06-02-codex-surfaces-enterprise-deployment-source-batch-review', 8, 'Enterprise Provider Placement',
  '### Enterprise Provider Placement

Amazon Bedrock support matters when a user or organization already needs AWS
identity, region control, VPC isolation, CloudTrail, KMS/encryption, procurement
or existing cloud commitments. It should trigger provider-placement questions:

- Must inference stay inside AWS governance?
- Which AWS account, region and identity boundary applies?
- Are required Codex capabilities available through this provider path?
- Which features are unavailable compared with OpenAI-hosted Codex?
- Who owns AWS cost, logs, access review and credential rotation?', 'c2d11d6d17635f804e07e437870bd6e9f0c836c584ef0a72cda1259a6f54ca16', 107
);
INSERT INTO chunks_fts (text, heading, document_id, chunk_id)
VALUES ('### Enterprise Provider Placement

Amazon Bedrock support matters when a user or organization already needs AWS
identity, region control, VPC isolation, CloudTrail, KMS/encryption, procurement
or existing cloud commitments. It should trigger provider-placement questions:

- Must inference stay inside AWS governance?
- Which AWS account, region and identity boundary applies?
- Are required Codex capabilities available through this provider path?
- Which features are unavailable compared with OpenAI-hosted Codex?
- Who owns AWS cost, logs, access review and credential rotation?', 'Enterprise Provider Placement', '2026-06-02-codex-surfaces-enterprise-deployment-source-batch-review', '2026-06-02-codex-surfaces-enterprise-deployment-source-batch-review#8');

INSERT INTO chunks (id, document_id, ordinal, heading, text, hash, token_count)
VALUES (
  '2026-06-02-codex-surfaces-enterprise-deployment-source-batch-review#9', '2026-06-02-codex-surfaces-enterprise-deployment-source-batch-review', 9, 'Shared Agent Governance',
  '### Shared Agent Governance

Workspace agents confirm that shared agents are different from personal local
agents. If a Pritha descendant will be shared by a team, run in Slack, work on a
schedule or operate across business tools, the contract must include ownership,
permissions, approvals, analytics, audit logs, escalation paths and user-facing
handoff rules.', '38d3247b22f21c05b5b9e7c492440ebbd55db644e815098fc931898790dec5c5', 73
);
INSERT INTO chunks_fts (text, heading, document_id, chunk_id)
VALUES ('### Shared Agent Governance

Workspace agents confirm that shared agents are different from personal local
agents. If a Pritha descendant will be shared by a team, run in Slack, work on a
schedule or operate across business tools, the contract must include ownership,
permissions, approvals, analytics, audit logs, escalation paths and user-facing
handoff rules.', 'Shared Agent Governance', '2026-06-02-codex-surfaces-enterprise-deployment-source-batch-review', '2026-06-02-codex-surfaces-enterprise-deployment-source-batch-review#9');

INSERT INTO chunks (id, document_id, ordinal, heading, text, hash, token_count)
VALUES (
  '2026-06-02-codex-surfaces-enterprise-deployment-source-batch-review#10', '2026-06-02-codex-surfaces-enterprise-deployment-source-batch-review', 10, 'Relationship To Existing Memory',
  '## Relationship To Existing Memory

- Reinforces `agent-creation-harness` and the existing OpenAI harness
  assessment.
- Refines `agent-shell-evaluation`: Codex is a family of surfaces, not a single
  shell.
- Refines `agent-runtime-placement`: Bedrock is a provider/deployment path with
  different capability and governance constraints.
- Refines `agent-mcp-connector-lifecycle`: gateways and catalogs do not remove
  pre-flight tool boundary selection.
- Compatible with `agent-skill-pack-lifecycle`: skills remain selectable
  procedural memory, whether used locally, in Codex, or in workspace agents.', '89470be6a36548d28c6fab2c2cf19d0f3ddf151d038c52a3e1e9eb932d601f53', 98
);
INSERT INTO chunks_fts (text, heading, document_id, chunk_id)
VALUES ('## Relationship To Existing Memory

- Reinforces `agent-creation-harness` and the existing OpenAI harness
  assessment.
- Refines `agent-shell-evaluation`: Codex is a family of surfaces, not a single
  shell.
- Refines `agent-runtime-placement`: Bedrock is a provider/deployment path with
  different capability and governance constraints.
- Refines `agent-mcp-connector-lifecycle`: gateways and catalogs do not remove
  pre-flight tool boundary selection.
- Compatible with `agent-skill-pack-lifecycle`: skills remain selectable
  procedural memory, whether used locally, in Codex, or in workspace agents.', 'Relationship To Existing Memory', '2026-06-02-codex-surfaces-enterprise-deployment-source-batch-review', '2026-06-02-codex-surfaces-enterprise-deployment-source-batch-review#10');

INSERT INTO chunks (id, document_id, ordinal, heading, text, hash, token_count)
VALUES (
  '2026-06-02-codex-surfaces-enterprise-deployment-source-batch-review#11', '2026-06-02-codex-surfaces-enterprise-deployment-source-batch-review', 11, 'Techscope Adoption Check',
  '## Techscope Adoption Check

- Techscope/Agents Mother fit: adopt.
- Implementation cost: low for standards and contract fields, medium for
  scaffold checks, high for full SDK orchestration and enterprise Bedrock
  deployment automation.
- Operational complexity: medium to high depending on provider and MCP scope.
- Risk: over-expanding tool surfaces, confusing Codex surfaces, assuming
  Bedrock parity, or treating workspace agents as equivalent to local
  descendants.
- Decision: update standards now; add deeper scaffold automation only when a
  concrete child-agent contract selects the corresponding module.', '2be18b58aa24fcd889dce91a5c0d76dd5cc1c2afca93ca1b5b28e65125bc4990', 113
);
INSERT INTO chunks_fts (text, heading, document_id, chunk_id)
VALUES ('## Techscope Adoption Check

