INSERT INTO chunks_fts (text, heading, document_id, chunk_id)
VALUES ('# Review: JS/TS Agent UI Framework Source Batch

Date: 2026-06-02
Status: draft
Recommendation: standard-update', 'Review: JS/TS Agent UI Framework Source Batch', '2026-06-02-js-ts-agent-ui-framework-source-batch-review', '2026-06-02-js-ts-agent-ui-framework-source-batch-review#1');

INSERT INTO chunks (id, document_id, ordinal, heading, text, hash, token_count)
VALUES (
  '2026-06-02-js-ts-agent-ui-framework-source-batch-review#2', '2026-06-02-js-ts-agent-ui-framework-source-batch-review', 2, 'One-Paragraph Read',
  '## One-Paragraph Read

This batch is useful only after filtering. Most named materials are about
JavaScript/TypeScript agent backends, not UI frameworks. For Pritha''s UI layer,
the durable point is that agent UIs need streaming state, typed tool rendering,
approval controls, cancellation, error states, persistence/resume and
framework-compatible hooks/components. Vercel AI SDK UI is the strongest direct
UI source in the batch. LangChain.js, Google ADK TS, OpenAI Agents SDK TS and
Mastra should be treated as runtime/harness candidates unless the child-agent
contract explicitly needs their frontend integration.', '680241121675ea6708646fbb3236a0b722af42477bb7eef4ed3954282c554349', 115
);
INSERT INTO chunks_fts (text, heading, document_id, chunk_id)
VALUES ('## One-Paragraph Read

This batch is useful only after filtering. Most named materials are about
JavaScript/TypeScript agent backends, not UI frameworks. For Pritha''s UI layer,
the durable point is that agent UIs need streaming state, typed tool rendering,
approval controls, cancellation, error states, persistence/resume and
framework-compatible hooks/components. Vercel AI SDK UI is the strongest direct
UI source in the batch. LangChain.js, Google ADK TS, OpenAI Agents SDK TS and
Mastra should be treated as runtime/harness candidates unless the child-agent
contract explicitly needs their frontend integration.', 'One-Paragraph Read', '2026-06-02-js-ts-agent-ui-framework-source-batch-review', '2026-06-02-js-ts-agent-ui-framework-source-batch-review#2');

INSERT INTO chunks (id, document_id, ordinal, heading, text, hash, token_count)
VALUES (
  '2026-06-02-js-ts-agent-ui-framework-source-batch-review#3', '2026-06-02-js-ts-agent-ui-framework-source-batch-review', 3, 'Source Verdicts',
  '## Source Verdicts

| Date | Source | UI verdict | Pritha fit |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| 2026-04-23 | Microsoft LangChain.js course | backend/context only | Good JS onboarding for tools/agents/RAG, but not a UI framework decision source. |
| 2025-12-22 | Vercel AI SDK 6 | adopt for UI principles | Strong TS/UI pattern: framework support, typed UI messages/tool parts, streaming, approvals, DevTools. |
| current docs | AI SDK UI | adopt | Direct UI hooks for chat, completion, structured objects, status/error state and framework support. |
| 2025-12-17 | Google ADK TypeScript | backend/context only | Code-first agent framework; useful for runtime selection, not UI framework selection. |
| current docs | OpenAI Agents SDK TypeScript | backend/context only | Runtime for text/sandbox/voice agents; UI relevance only through voice/browser integrations and external app design. |
| 2025-04-19 | Mastra JS framework comparison | backend/context only | Helps choose agent orchestration style, not frontend UI layer. |', 'd7a721547ce5757a6cedc9b64e073778a6151f63258a7b9e1b0bfb71368a11f7', 225
);
INSERT INTO chunks_fts (text, heading, document_id, chunk_id)
VALUES ('## Source Verdicts

| Date | Source | UI verdict | Pritha fit |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| 2026-04-23 | Microsoft LangChain.js course | backend/context only | Good JS onboarding for tools/agents/RAG, but not a UI framework decision source. |
| 2025-12-22 | Vercel AI SDK 6 | adopt for UI principles | Strong TS/UI pattern: framework support, typed UI messages/tool parts, streaming, approvals, DevTools. |
| current docs | AI SDK UI | adopt | Direct UI hooks for chat, completion, structured objects, status/error state and framework support. |
| 2025-12-17 | Google ADK TypeScript | backend/context only | Code-first agent framework; useful for runtime selection, not UI framework selection. |
| current docs | OpenAI Agents SDK TypeScript | backend/context only | Runtime for text/sandbox/voice agents; UI relevance only through voice/browser integrations and external app design. |
| 2025-04-19 | Mastra JS framework comparison | backend/context only | Helps choose agent orchestration style, not frontend UI layer. |', 'Source Verdicts', '2026-06-02-js-ts-agent-ui-framework-source-batch-review', '2026-06-02-js-ts-agent-ui-framework-source-batch-review#3');

INSERT INTO chunks (id, document_id, ordinal, heading, text, hash, token_count)
VALUES (
  '2026-06-02-js-ts-agent-ui-framework-source-batch-review#4', '2026-06-02-js-ts-agent-ui-framework-source-batch-review', 4, 'UI Principles To Keep',
  '## UI Principles To Keep

- Start from the user''s workflow, not from the agent backend.
- Preserve the existing frontend stack unless the contract needs a new surface.
- Use a framework-compatible AI UI layer when it reduces streaming, message
  state, tool rendering and error-handling complexity.
- Render tool calls as typed components when the user must inspect data,
  approve actions or compare structured results.
- Expose status states such as submitted, streaming, ready and error.
- Provide stop/cancel, regenerate/retry and resume/persistence when tasks can
  run longer than one response.
- Keep agent runtime internals behind an adapter. The UI should consume stable
  message/tool/state events, not raw framework traces.', 'b1314d8db961973a711e7eea504746316457eeb2f8c8cd8e30b8b44dfd0358ee', 149
);
INSERT INTO chunks_fts (text, heading, document_id, chunk_id)
VALUES ('## UI Principles To Keep

- Start from the user''s workflow, not from the agent backend.
- Preserve the existing frontend stack unless the contract needs a new surface.
- Use a framework-compatible AI UI layer when it reduces streaming, message
  state, tool rendering and error-handling complexity.
- Render tool calls as typed components when the user must inspect data,
  approve actions or compare structured results.
- Expose status states such as submitted, streaming, ready and error.
- Provide stop/cancel, regenerate/retry and resume/persistence when tasks can
  run longer than one response.
- Keep agent runtime internals behind an adapter. The UI should consume stable
  message/tool/state events, not raw framework traces.', 'UI Principles To Keep', '2026-06-02-js-ts-agent-ui-framework-source-batch-review', '2026-06-02-js-ts-agent-ui-framework-source-batch-review#4');

INSERT INTO chunks (id, document_id, ordinal, heading, text, hash, token_count)
VALUES (
  '2026-06-02-js-ts-agent-ui-framework-source-batch-review#5', '2026-06-02-js-ts-agent-ui-framework-source-batch-review', 5, 'Techscope Adoption Check',
  '## Techscope Adoption Check

- Techscope/Agents Mother fit: adopt as a standard update.
- Implementation cost: low for contract/standard fields; medium if adding a
  reusable Next.js/Vercel AI SDK scaffold later.
- Operational complexity: low for chat UI, medium for tool approval/generative
  UI, high if UI controls real side effects.
- Current architecture impact: update `agent-interface-experience`; do not
  select a default JS backend.
- Decision: keep Vercel AI SDK UI as a candidate frontend layer for
  TypeScript/web child agents, but avoid promoting LangChain.js, ADK TS,
  OpenAI Agents SDK TS or Mastra as UI defaults.', '7bab04fbb678739b26b31741326ca670dbea393a0b9d86b700345f6dfb035e91', 126
);
INSERT INTO chunks_fts (text, heading, document_id, chunk_id)
VALUES ('## Techscope Adoption Check

- Techscope/Agents Mother fit: adopt as a standard update.
- Implementation cost: low for contract/standard fields; medium if adding a
  reusable Next.js/Vercel AI SDK scaffold later.
- Operational complexity: low for chat UI, medium for tool approval/generative
  UI, high if UI controls real side effects.
- Current architecture impact: update `agent-interface-experience`; do not
  select a default JS backend.
- Decision: keep Vercel AI SDK UI as a candidate frontend layer for
  TypeScript/web child agents, but avoid promoting LangChain.js, ADK TS,
  OpenAI Agents SDK TS or Mastra as UI defaults.', 'Techscope Adoption Check', '2026-06-02-js-ts-agent-ui-framework-source-batch-review', '2026-06-02-js-ts-agent-ui-framework-source-batch-review#5');

INSERT INTO chunks (id, document_id, ordinal, heading, text, hash, token_count)
VALUES (
  '2026-06-02-js-ts-agent-ui-framework-source-batch-review#6', '2026-06-02-js-ts-agent-ui-framework-source-batch-review', 6, 'Promotion Guidance',
  '## Promotion Guidance

Promote:

- existing frontend framework first;
- AI UI layer selected by user-facing state/control needs;
- typed UI messages and tool components;
- visible status/error/cancel/regenerate controls;
- approval UI for side-effect tools;
- framework-agnostic adapter between runtime and UI.

Do not promote:

- backend agent framework as UI framework;
- Node/TypeScript as a reason to choose web UI;
- Vercel/Next as universal default;
- direct browser access to secrets or agent runtime internals;
- UI changes that lack mobile/accessibility verification.', '8809612ae98d7a8eaf1caaaf2e538ea1e44291a400be2e957a660953fa32d8bf', 113
);
INSERT INTO chunks_fts (text, heading, document_id, chunk_id)
VALUES ('## Promotion Guidance

Promote:

- existing frontend framework first;
- AI UI layer selected by user-facing state/control needs;
- typed UI messages and tool components;
- visible status/error/cancel/regenerate controls;
- approval UI for side-effect tools;
- framework-agnostic adapter between runtime and UI.

Do not promote:

- backend agent framework as UI framework;
- Node/TypeScript as a reason to choose web UI;
- Vercel/Next as universal default;
- direct browser access to secrets or agent runtime internals;
- UI changes that lack mobile/accessibility verification.', 'Promotion Guidance', '2026-06-02-js-ts-agent-ui-framework-source-batch-review', '2026-06-02-js-ts-agent-ui-framework-source-batch-review#6');

