INSERT INTO chunks (id, document_id, ordinal, heading, text, hash, token_count)
VALUES (
  'memory-domains#2', 'memory-domains', 2, 'Rule',
  '## Rule

Pritha memory uses two independent axes:

- folder/stage: maturity of knowledge;
- memory domain: semantic area of meaning.

Do not replace the current staged Markdown architecture with domain folders.
Add domain metadata so a single artifact can belong to several domains.', '7e2b6e0e367ba6f269430358edd1b9f352204aa8117799ea2e8b44c4a23152bb', 59
);
INSERT INTO chunks_fts (text, heading, document_id, chunk_id)
VALUES ('## Rule

Pritha memory uses two independent axes:

- folder/stage: maturity of knowledge;
- memory domain: semantic area of meaning.

Do not replace the current staged Markdown architecture with domain folders.
Add domain metadata so a single artifact can belong to several domains.', 'Rule', 'memory-domains', 'memory-domains#2');

INSERT INTO chunks (id, document_id, ordinal, heading, text, hash, token_count)
VALUES (
  'memory-domains#3', 'memory-domains', 3, 'Canonical Domains',
  '## Canonical Domains

| Domain | Meaning |
| --- | --- |
| `pritha-self` | Pritha identity, capabilities, limits, roadmap, lifecycle and self-improvement. |
| `child-agents` | Created descendants, contracts, reports, profiles, lifecycle evidence and lessons. |
| `agent-building-knowledge` | General patterns for harnesses, memory, tools, skills, MCP, runtime placement, interfaces and operations. |
| `user-model` | User preferences and working model. Must be local-private unless explicitly exported. |
| `source-material` | Intake, source notes, signals and processed source-derived knowledge. |
| `governance` | Standards, decisions, safety, privacy, promotion rules and audit policies. |
| `marketing` | Pritha product narrative, positioning, myths, stories, taglines and public-facing copy drafts. |', '88de0e125b630a174b8d6e6e968c3571f2c703dacc368770a93c9cdbf9fe1156', 149
);
INSERT INTO chunks_fts (text, heading, document_id, chunk_id)
VALUES ('## Canonical Domains

| Domain | Meaning |
| --- | --- |
| `pritha-self` | Pritha identity, capabilities, limits, roadmap, lifecycle and self-improvement. |
| `child-agents` | Created descendants, contracts, reports, profiles, lifecycle evidence and lessons. |
| `agent-building-knowledge` | General patterns for harnesses, memory, tools, skills, MCP, runtime placement, interfaces and operations. |
| `user-model` | User preferences and working model. Must be local-private unless explicitly exported. |
| `source-material` | Intake, source notes, signals and processed source-derived knowledge. |
| `governance` | Standards, decisions, safety, privacy, promotion rules and audit policies. |
| `marketing` | Pritha product narrative, positioning, myths, stories, taglines and public-facing copy drafts. |', 'Canonical Domains', 'memory-domains', 'memory-domains#3');

INSERT INTO chunks (id, document_id, ordinal, heading, text, hash, token_count)
VALUES (
  'memory-domains#4', 'memory-domains', 4, 'Frontmatter Convention',
  '## Frontmatter Convention

Use these fields for new curated artifacts when the domain is clear:

```yaml
memory_domain: agent-building-knowledge
memory_domains:
  - agent-building-knowledge
  - governance
subject:
  kind: pattern
  id: agent-harness-evaluation
privacy: public
retention: durable
review_status: draft
confidence: medium
```

`memory_domain` is the primary domain. `memory_domains` lists all relevant
domains. `subject.kind` and `subject.id` identify what the artifact is about.', 'f93bc343b1a59eb59a23eaac9597ff57d071eea6468ebe6a09bbc0d6841e52a1', 76
);
