INSERT INTO chunks_fts (text, heading, document_id, chunk_id)
VALUES ('# Decision: Pritha Memory Domain Model

Date: 2026-06-02
Status: accepted', 'Decision: Pritha Memory Domain Model', '2026-06-02-pritha-memory-domain-model', '2026-06-02-pritha-memory-domain-model#1');

INSERT INTO chunks (id, document_id, ordinal, heading, text, hash, token_count)
VALUES (
  '2026-06-02-pritha-memory-domain-model#2', '2026-06-02-pritha-memory-domain-model', 2, 'Context',
  '## Context

Pritha''s current memory architecture already has a useful staged structure:
inbox, sources, signals, briefs, reviews, standards, decisions, workflows,
generated wiki and agent lifecycle reports. Replacing this with domain folders
would make the system more brittle because one artifact can belong to several
semantic areas at once.

The useful improvement is to add a semantic domain layer over existing
Markdown/frontmatter and SQLite indexing.', '97c25a2aaa89cde89ce73b5cb311e1d932fe1d195d69ce5b53c4c221bcd9497e', 87
);
INSERT INTO chunks_fts (text, heading, document_id, chunk_id)
VALUES ('## Context

Pritha''s current memory architecture already has a useful staged structure:
inbox, sources, signals, briefs, reviews, standards, decisions, workflows,
generated wiki and agent lifecycle reports. Replacing this with domain folders
would make the system more brittle because one artifact can belong to several
semantic areas at once.

The useful improvement is to add a semantic domain layer over existing
Markdown/frontmatter and SQLite indexing.', 'Context', '2026-06-02-pritha-memory-domain-model', '2026-06-02-pritha-memory-domain-model#2');

INSERT INTO chunks (id, document_id, ordinal, heading, text, hash, token_count)
VALUES (
  '2026-06-02-pritha-memory-domain-model#3', '2026-06-02-pritha-memory-domain-model', 3, 'Decision',
  '## Decision

Adopt `memory_domain`, `memory_domains`, `subject`, `privacy`, `retention`,
`review_status` and `confidence` as optional-but-preferred frontmatter fields
for new curated artifacts.

Use these canonical domains:

- `pritha-self`;
- `child-agents`;
- `agent-building-knowledge`;
- `user-model`;
- `source-material`;
- `governance`;
- `marketing`.

Keep the current physical folder structure as the primary knowledge maturity
model. Add one new physical section, `12_marketing/`, for Pritha marketing copy,
myths, stories and product narrative drafts.', 'ad9cfaef9dfac40dcd617c14593e52e6705ee6f3e2e2a240755d469a06f3e745', 88
);
INSERT INTO chunks_fts (text, heading, document_id, chunk_id)
VALUES ('## Decision

Adopt `memory_domain`, `memory_domains`, `subject`, `privacy`, `retention`,
`review_status` and `confidence` as optional-but-preferred frontmatter fields
for new curated artifacts.

Use these canonical domains:

- `pritha-self`;
- `child-agents`;
- `agent-building-knowledge`;
- `user-model`;
- `source-material`;
- `governance`;
- `marketing`.

Keep the current physical folder structure as the primary knowledge maturity
model. Add one new physical section, `12_marketing/`, for Pritha marketing copy,
myths, stories and product narrative drafts.', 'Decision', '2026-06-02-pritha-memory-domain-model', '2026-06-02-pritha-memory-domain-model#3');

INSERT INTO chunks (id, document_id, ordinal, heading, text, hash, token_count)
VALUES (
  '2026-06-02-pritha-memory-domain-model#4', '2026-06-02-pritha-memory-domain-model', 4, 'Consequences',
  '## Consequences

- Pritha can answer domain-shaped questions without moving files.
- Child-agent creation can retrieve standards/patterns first and past agents as
  evidence, not as templates to copy.
- User memory is explicitly separated from the public/portable Git snapshot.
- Marketing/identity material has a home without contaminating standards.', '3dac946b6d49b9cec1567099ffcbe11ddab5861f6459c4cbc25fd56ce29c8559', 65
);
INSERT INTO chunks_fts (text, heading, document_id, chunk_id)
VALUES ('## Consequences

- Pritha can answer domain-shaped questions without moving files.
- Child-agent creation can retrieve standards/patterns first and past agents as
  evidence, not as templates to copy.
- User memory is explicitly separated from the public/portable Git snapshot.
- Marketing/identity material has a home without contaminating standards.', 'Consequences', '2026-06-02-pritha-memory-domain-model', '2026-06-02-pritha-memory-domain-model#4');

INSERT INTO chunks (id, document_id, ordinal, heading, text, hash, token_count)
VALUES (
  '2026-06-02-pritha-memory-domain-model#5', '2026-06-02-pritha-memory-domain-model', 5, 'Alternatives considered',
  '## Alternatives considered

- Move files into `memory/pritha-self`, `memory/child-agents`, and similar
  folders: rejected because it would confuse maturity stage with semantic
  domain.
- Create separate databases for every domain: rejected for v1; too heavy before
  domain metadata proves useful.
- Automatically infer domains for every historical file: deferred; new curated
  artifacts should lead the migration.', '03116ea979f96c236bd85fa1c3c169b0d1c38c7cbc353109ec9db8264e25a741', 75
);
INSERT INTO chunks_fts (text, heading, document_id, chunk_id)
VALUES ('## Alternatives considered

- Move files into `memory/pritha-self`, `memory/child-agents`, and similar
