INSERT INTO chunks (id, document_id, ordinal, heading, text, hash, token_count)
VALUES (
  '2026-06-01-fespa26-funny-teacher-tailscale-serve-recovery-report#6', '2026-06-01-fespa26-funny-teacher-tailscale-serve-recovery-report', 6, 'Recovery Pattern',
  '## Recovery Pattern

When multiple local agents share Tailscale Serve:

1. Preserve the known-good reference service and do not edit its project files during network diagnosis.
2. Reset Tailscale Serve to the smallest needed mapping.
3. Verify local upstream health.
4. Verify tailnet URL from the host, while remembering that host self-access is not enough.
5. If peers still cannot open the service but `tailscale ping` works, restart Tailscale on the host and reapply Serve mappings.
6. Add additional services one at a time on separate HTTPS ports.
7. Record the final `tailscale serve status` shape.', 'ec19c093baa716b129dce4d64c2c2710b32a975de16f8b47a15681f597ba05a0', 130
);
INSERT INTO chunks_fts (text, heading, document_id, chunk_id)
VALUES ('## Recovery Pattern

When multiple local agents share Tailscale Serve:

1. Preserve the known-good reference service and do not edit its project files during network diagnosis.
2. Reset Tailscale Serve to the smallest needed mapping.
3. Verify local upstream health.
4. Verify tailnet URL from the host, while remembering that host self-access is not enough.
5. If peers still cannot open the service but `tailscale ping` works, restart Tailscale on the host and reapply Serve mappings.
6. Add additional services one at a time on separate HTTPS ports.
7. Record the final `tailscale serve status` shape.', 'Recovery Pattern', '2026-06-01-fespa26-funny-teacher-tailscale-serve-recovery-report', '2026-06-01-fespa26-funny-teacher-tailscale-serve-recovery-report#6');

INSERT INTO chunks (id, document_id, ordinal, heading, text, hash, token_count)
VALUES (
  '2026-06-01-fespa26-funny-teacher-tailscale-serve-recovery-report#7', '2026-06-01-fespa26-funny-teacher-tailscale-serve-recovery-report', 7, 'Commands',
  '## Commands

Reference command shape used for the stable state:

```sh
tailscale serve reset
tailscale serve --bg --https=3026 http://127.0.0.1:3027
tailscale serve --bg --https=3034 http://127.0.0.1:3033
tailscale serve status
```

When peer access is stuck even though local health and `tailscale ping` are good:

```sh
tailscale down
sleep 3
tailscale up
tailscale serve --bg --https=3026 http://127.0.0.1:3027
tailscale serve --bg --https=3034 http://127.0.0.1:3033
```', '891637d0026bdc01b4c9de54a92c6b89b2387acd6f26da6b7ff5357f0cd6eb63', 81
);
INSERT INTO chunks_fts (text, heading, document_id, chunk_id)
VALUES ('## Commands

Reference command shape used for the stable state:

```sh
tailscale serve reset
tailscale serve --bg --https=3026 http://127.0.0.1:3027
tailscale serve --bg --https=3034 http://127.0.0.1:3033
tailscale serve status
```

When peer access is stuck even though local health and `tailscale ping` are good:

```sh
tailscale down
sleep 3
tailscale up
tailscale serve --bg --https=3026 http://127.0.0.1:3027
tailscale serve --bg --https=3034 http://127.0.0.1:3033
```', 'Commands', '2026-06-01-fespa26-funny-teacher-tailscale-serve-recovery-report', '2026-06-01-fespa26-funny-teacher-tailscale-serve-recovery-report#7');

INSERT INTO chunks (id, document_id, ordinal, heading, text, hash, token_count)
VALUES (
  '2026-06-01-fespa26-funny-teacher-tailscale-serve-recovery-report#8', '2026-06-01-fespa26-funny-teacher-tailscale-serve-recovery-report', 8, 'Lessons',
  '## Lessons

- Tailscale URL success from the host can be a misleading hairpin check; always confirm from the target device when mobile/laptop access matters.
- Restore the reference service before adding a second service.
- Keep each agent on a separate Tailscale HTTPS port to avoid path and cache ambiguity.
- Use health endpoints for each upstream before judging browser UI behavior.', '44b8132dc7338487a0fbf2c536366acefd1534bfbdc5c5e805f6de48ae484a36', 86
);
INSERT INTO chunks_fts (text, heading, document_id, chunk_id)
VALUES ('## Lessons

- Tailscale URL success from the host can be a misleading hairpin check; always confirm from the target device when mobile/laptop access matters.
- Restore the reference service before adding a second service.
- Keep each agent on a separate Tailscale HTTPS port to avoid path and cache ambiguity.
- Use health endpoints for each upstream before judging browser UI behavior.', 'Lessons', '2026-06-01-fespa26-funny-teacher-tailscale-serve-recovery-report', '2026-06-01-fespa26-funny-teacher-tailscale-serve-recovery-report#8');

